PVD("bangladesh_vision_2021-2041",{"docs":["","Bangladesh Vision Doc 2041"],"s":{"1":[[1,"225","5","Minimum Standards for Environmental and Water and Air Quality Protection","minimum standards are defined for such issues as environmental protection, water quality and air quality and these standards are monitored by the higher government.",""],[1,"229","2","Water and Sanitation Service Expansion and Regulation Reform","PP2041 strategy to address the water and sanitation problem is to sharply expand public services while also encouraging private supply.",""],[1,"229","2","Water and Sanitation Regulation and Cost Recovery Policy","This will be done by instituting proper regulations and appropriate cost recovery policy.",""],[1,"229","2","Waste and Sewage Disposal Regulation and Coordination Mechanism","Proper regulations for waste/sewage disposal and coordination with public waste/sewage treatment facilities are essential to preserve health safety.",""],[1,"229","3","Urban Sewage and Solid Waste Management Institutional Reform","a top priority for PP2041 is to institute adequate supply of modern sewage facilities in all cities.",""],[1,"229","3","WASA-Type Urban Water and Sewage Institutions","All City Corporations and larger Municipalities will be equipped with WASA type institutions that will have accountability for piped water supply and sewage disposal.",""],[1,"229","3","Municipal Solid Waste Management Capacity Development","Adequate capacity development of the municipalities including reformation of their organogram can be considered to plan, guide and monitor solid waste management.",""],[1,"229","3","WASA Reassignment to City Corporations","Existing WASAs would be re-assigned to the respective City Corporations where they provide service.",""],[1,"229","3","Urban LGI Accountability and Cost Recovery Strengthening","This is necessary to strengthen the accountability of the urban LGIs and make them responsive to the needs of the residents they oversee.",""],[1,"229","3","Urban Service Agency Cost Recovery Policy Strengthening","Cost recovery policies would be strengthened to improve the financial viability and service delivery capacity of these service agencies.",""],[1,"229","4","Modern Waste Treatment Facilities","Proper disposal of sewage and solid waste requires modern waste treatment facilities.","Ministries of LGRD and Environment"],[1,"230","4","National-City Coordination for Standards Implementation","But the implementation of these laws, regulations and standards will often require proper dialogue and consultation.","Local Government Division"]],"2":[[1,"14","5","Poverty Elimination and Social Protection Guarantee","by 2031 extreme poverty will be eliminated and by 2041 the incidence of poverty will be minimal (3% or less).",""],[1,"15","2","Expanded Social Safety Nets for Basic Needs","This will require additional funding to ensure social safety-net like food, clothing, shelter, health and education with an emphasis on quality and on eliminating the inequalities of access to relevant services for the poor.",""],[1,"15","2","Targeted Support for Vulnerable and Socially Excluded Groups","The government will escalate renewed efforts to address the most vulnerable, the most disadvantaged, the marginalized and the socially excluded section of the society.",""],[1,"15","2","Targeted Inclusion Support for Ethnic Minorities and Other Vulnerable Groups","Ethnic minorities living in the CHT and the plain districts will be given utmost attention.",""],[1,"15","2","Full Implementation of the NSSS for Vulnerable Groups","Efforts will be reinforced in taking care of the persons with disabilities, dalits, bede people, people living in slum areas and charland, street children, sex workers through full implementation of the NSSS.",""],[1,"66","2","Expanded Social Safety Net Network","The continued thrust on employment generation, promotion of human resource development, and a wider network of safety nets for the poor, elderly and disabled population will address this objective.",""],[1,"78","3","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","The National Social Security Strategy (NSSS 2015) recognized these challenges and incorporates new strategies (including a plan to introduce universal pension scheme), programmes and policies that address them and make social protection much more focused on the poor.",""],[1,"82","4","Accelerated Implementation of the National Social Security Strategy","The present system of social protection needs to be replaced with faster implementation of the NSSS.",""],[1,"83","1","Life-Cycle Based Core Programmes for the Poor and Vulnerable","The government funding for the NSSS will be focused on life-cycle based core programmes for the poor and the vulnerable.",""],[1,"83","1","Institutional and Administrative Reform for NSSS Efficiency","Required institutional and administrative reforms will be implemented to eliminate misuse and improve efficiency.",""],[1,"83","1","Cash-Based Online Transfer System for Social Protection","Most programmes will be cash-based and transferred on-line.",""],[1,"83","1","Management Information System for NSSS Beneficiary Identification and Monitoring","A proper MIS system will be instituted to identify beneficiaries and do M&E as an input to the continuous effort to improve the delivery of the NSSS.",""],[1,"83","2","Redistributive Fiscal Policy for Expanded Social Spending","Bangladesh will introduce a redistributive fiscal policy under PP2041 such that the level of spending on health, education and social protection will expand considerably.",""],[1,"83","2","Progressive Personal Income Tax Reform","These will be largely financed by an overhaul of the personal income taxation that is broad-based and progressive in nature.",""],[1,"83","4","Marginalized People Support Measures Beyond Social Protection","The government will continue to provide equal opportunities for all while taking measures for the marginalized people, beyond social protection.",""],[1,"84","2","Special Inclusion Programmes for Socially Excluded Groups","The government will undertake special programmes to improve their lives, provide access to training and education, health care, nutrition, sanitation, employment, aside from the provision of special treatment in government jobs and ensuring their fundamental human rights.",""]],"3":[[1,"183","3","ICT Division Development in the Ministry of Post and Telecommunication","The development of ICT division in the ministry of post and telecommunication has increased emphasis on ICT led progression of the economy","ministry of post and telecommunication"],[1,"184","7","National ICT Infrastructure Expansion","the government has undertaken initiatives to build ICT infrastructure, including four-tier national data centre, and establishing connectivity up to rural area of the country by laying fibre optics cable.",""],[1,"184","7","Digital Island Connectivity Initiative","The Government has connected Moheshkhali, one of the remotest islands of Bangladesh, to mainstream digital activities and services under the digital island initiative, and aims to replicate on other remote islands.",""],[1,"186","2","Last-Mile Connectivity Expansion by DoICT","initiative of Department of ICT (DoICT) to address last-mile connectivity",""],[1,"186","2","Digital Connectivity Expansion for DoCIT","Establishing Digital Connectivity of DoCIT will speed up the digitization progress further.",""],[1,"199","14","Information Infrastructure Development","Development of information infrastructure",""],[1,"199","14","Telecommunications and Internet Expansion","Expansion of tele & internet density",""],[1,"216","2","Communications Modernization and Media Expansion Support","PP2041 will build on this success and continue to modernize communications in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"216","2","Private Telecommunications Investment Support","The PP2041 strategy will continue to provide policy and institutional support to private investment in expanding telecommunications network and services, boost the expansion of private print, audio and video media, and provide an enabling environment for competitive and healthy expansion of communication services and knowledge and information sharing.",""]],"4":[[1,"111","1","Delta Plan 2100","That remains a major long-term challenge of Bangladesh agriculture and has been addressed as an integral part of the overall development agenda under the Government's Delta Plan 2100.",""],[1,"112","5","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Production Strategy","In the case of food production, climate change adaptation strategy in the agriculture sector needs to be prioritized to address the global food insecurity susceptibility due to climate change.",""],[1,"112","5","Post-Harvest Loss Reduction and Food Waste Minimization","Moreover, efforts should be taken to minimize the post-harvest loss and habitual wastages of valuable foods by rich people.",""],[1,"112","5","Sustainable Agricultural Intensification in Unfavourable Agro-Ecosystems","Six strategic approaches are called for: (a) Bringing unfavourable agri-ecosystem under productive sustainable agricultural practices;",""],[1,"112","5","Crop Intensification with Soil Health Sustainability","(b) Intensification of crop cultivation in productive agricultural land maintaining sustainability of soil health;",""],[1,"112","5","Sustainable Agricultural Production Intensification","(c) Sustainably Intensifying Agricultural Production Systems without bringing new land under cultivation;",""],[1,"113","1","Climate-Resilient Crop and Livestock Production Systems","Increasing Resilience of crop and livestock production systems in the face of climate change;",""],[1,"113","1","Agricultural and Livelihood Diversification","Diversification in agricultural output and livelihoods involving more plant species or varieties, or animal breeds, off-farm activities and employment;",""],[1,"113","1","Adaptive Response Development for Climate Uncertainty","Coping with Uncertainty in Developing Responses due to uncertainty about the scale and eventual nature of adaptation needed to address climate change.",""],[1,"114","2","Crop Zoning and Precision Agriculture Promotion","Production program will have to be organized based on crop zoning, with a move to adopt precision agriculture practices wherever possible.",""],[1,"116","4","Agricultural Research Strengthening and Technology Scaling Programme","This has to be strengthened and adequately funded to address the problem areas (like hills, coastal, haor and barind areas) that are more prone to weather vagaries and that have proportionately higher populations of poor and vulnerable people.",""],[1,"117","6","Agricultural Production Efficiency and Waste Reduction Measures","Improving the efficiency of agricultural production systems, increasing sequestration, and reducing wastes will generate higher and more stable returns from farming investments.",""],[1,"117","15","Agricultural Research Institute Strengthening","Strengthening of agricultural research institute will be given the highest priority.",""],[1,"121","1","Climate Adaptation and Mitigation Measures","Adaptation and mitigation measures will have to be taken now to ensure sustainable agriculture and rural livelihoods.",""],[1,"121","1","Adaptive Capacity Building in Climate-Sensitive Sectors","Building and improving adaptive capacity and taking technical and non-technical adaptation actions in key climate-sensitive sectors such as agriculture must be an urgent priority for Bangladesh.",""],[1,"121","1","Adaptation Actions in Soil, Water, Forestry, and Coastal Resources","There is also the need for making strong efforts in taking adaptation actions in key related sectors including soil and water resources, forestry, coastal and marine resources.",""],[1,"121","2","Climate Information and Weather Forecasting Services","providing public goods and services, such as better climate information and weather forecasting",""],[1,"121","2","Heat-Resistant Crop Research and Development","research and development on heat- resistant crop varieties and climate-smart techniques",""],[1,"121","2","Agricultural Early Warning Systems","early warning systems",""],[1,"121","2","Livestock Species and Fodder Variety Exploration","search for potential livestock species and fodder varieties",""],[1,"121","2","Index-Based Agricultural Insurance Schemes","explore innovative risk-sharing instruments such as index-based insurance schemes of commercial ventures",""],[1,"121","7","Climate Change Adaptation Incentives and Policy Framework","The Government has a vital role to play in providing incentives and an effective policy framework for individuals and firms to adapt to climate change and to enhance their adaptive capacity.",""],[1,"122","1","Adaptive Capacity Support for Vulnerable Groups and Localities","There is also a need for adopting a more holistic approach to building the adaptive capacity of vulnerable groups and localities (e.g. in Coastal Zone Hotspot) in rural as well as urban areas to build their resilience to shocks, including developing their capability to diversify local economies, livelihoods, and coping strategies.",""],[1,"158","5","Proactive Long-Term Employment Strategy for Industry 4.0","it would be advisable to adopt a pro-active policy so that the economy can benefit from the positive aspects of new and better jobs.",""]],"5":[[1,"12","1","Cross-Cutting Policy Coordination and Multi-Sector Program Synchronization","Achieving high growth with shared prosperity requires coordination of cross-cutting policies and synchronization of multi-sectoral programs aimed at achieving the final outcome.",""],[1,"13","1","Institutional Capacity Building for a Transforming Economy","The fourth pillar is institutional capacity building.",""],[1,"42","3","Institution Building for Inclusive and Sustainable Growth","programs and institutions will have to be put in place to generate rapid, inclusive and sustainable growth",""],[1,"48","2","Governance Improvement and Public Service Quality Enhancement","These are (i) governance; (ii) democratization; (iii) decentralization and (iv) capacity building.",""],[1,"48","2","Public Sector Capacity Building Initiative","increasing the capabilities of those working for different relevant organizations in order make them work better",""],[1,"53","1","Public Sector Reform and Institutional Strengthening","Reform-minded governments should seize opportunities to build consensus, address the obstacles to change, and initiate and sustain reforms to build an effective public sector.",""],[1,"54","3","Institutional Strengthening Agenda","The strategic thrust of PP2041 will be on strengthening institutions.",""],[1,"54","7","Strengthening Core Governance Institutions","Emphasis has to be on strengthening core governance institutions like Comptroller and Auditor General, Public Accounts Committee, Bangladesh Bank, Public Service Commission, Securities and Exchange Commission, courts, local government bodies.",""],[1,"55","1","Governance Reforms to Attract Private Investment","In order to attract private investment including foreign private investment required to reach the bold 2041 income target, particular attention has to be paid to financial governance, fiscal governance, land governance, urban governance, corporate governance and the court system to enforce contracts and adjudicate disputes.",""],[1,"55","2","Governance Reform through Administrative Reform","Initiating governance reform for improvement of effectiveness through administrative reform as a continuing and gradual process",""],[1,"55","3","Effective Government and Rule of Law Continuation","Continuation of the strategy of effective government and enforcement of the rule of law with complete transparency and accountability within the framework of pluralistic democracy and further emphasis on e-governance.",""],[1,"56","3","Institutional Capacity Building for Economic Transformation","The fourth pillar of Vision 2041 is capacity building.",""],[1,"56","4","Civil Servant Training Expansion Initiative","A massive program of training, domestic and international, is underway.",""]],"6":[[1,"21","5","Least-Cost Power Generation Expansion Path","Adopting a least-cost power generation expansion path",""],[1,"21","5","Low-Cost Primary Energy Supply Promotion","Promoting supply of low-cost primary energy",""],[1,"21","5","Primary Fuel Infrastructure Development","Developing the required infrastructure for primary fuel",""],[1,"21","5","Balanced Power Sector Investment Allocation","Ensuring investment balance between generation, transmission and distribution",""],[1,"21","5","Installed Capacity Efficiency Improvement","Promoting efficient use of installed capacity",""],[1,"21","5","Private Investment Promotion in Energy","Promoting private investment in energy",""],[1,"21","5","Power Trade Expansion","Further expanding power trade",""],[1,"21","5","Energy Pricing Policy Reform","Ensuring proper energy pricing policy",""],[1,"21","5","Power and Energy Institutional Strengthening","Strengthening power and energy institutions",""],[1,"22","1","Power Expansion Strategy Development and Periodic Update","The PP2041 will develop a power expansion strategy in line with the 2016 PSMP and update this strategy every 5 years based on the lessons of experience.",""],[1,"22","2","Balanced Power Generation and Grid Investment Programme","power generation must be balanced with proper investments in transmission and distribution.",""],[1,"22","2","Private Sector Participation in Power Sector Expansion","PP2041 will build on this to enhance private involvement in power generation, transmission and distribution.",""],[1,"22","2","Regional Power Trade Expansion","Bangladesh will seek to considerably expand power trade options at competitive prices from all three neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"22","2","Cross-Border Electricity Import Diversification","The broadening of imports from Bhutan and Nepal will also help lower the risk of power supply disruption from conflict and accidents.",""],[1,"22","2","Large-Scale Power Capacity Expansion Programme","The generation programmed over the 20 years between FY2021 and FY2041 calls for a massive 62 thousand MW of capacity build up, which is an annual average expansion of 3100 MW per year.",""],[1,"175","4","Power Generation Capacity Expansion","The rapid expansion in power generation and associated investments in transmission, distribution and energy supply infrastructures will require a huge amount of resources.",""],[1,"176","1","Power and Energy Financing Strategy","the PP2041 financing strategy for power and energy consist of the following:",""],[1,"176","2","Strengthening Private Financing Support for Power Generation","Ongoing support programmes like IDCOL and Investment Financing Facility for Private sector (IFFP) will be further strengthened.",""],[1,"176","4","Budgetary Financing for Power and Energy Infrastructure","In the interim years, budgetary financing will remain dominant, especially for financing large power plants and for transmission and distribution networks and for the energy supply-related infrastructure.",""]],"7":[[1,"15","3","Knowledge-Based Economy Development","Specifically, the programme comprises the following: (a) Institution of a knowledge-based economy;",""],[1,"15","3","Universal Literacy Programme","Specifically, the programme comprises the following: (b) Population with 100% literacy rate;",""],[1,"15","3","Universal Free Education Through Grade 12","Specifically, the programme comprises the following: (c) Universal free education for up to 12 years;",""],[1,"16","1","Quality Improvement in Education Delivery Systems","For both delivery system, emphasis on quality will be the major theme.",""],[1,"34","10","Higher Education Quality Enhancement Project","Higher Education Quality Enhancement Project",""]],"8":[[1,"212","9","Inland Water Transport Development Strategy","The PP2041 will seek to harness this potential for both passenger and cargo traffic.",""],[1,"212","10","Priority Routing and River Port Infrastructure Development","Establish priority routing based on potential passenger and freight traffic flows and develop those navigability improvements and river port infrastructures.",""],[1,"212","11","River Route Navigability Improvement","Sharply improve the navigability of river routes through strategic dredging, river training, and bandalling.",""],[1,"212","12","Inter-Regional River Connectivity Enhancement","Give priority to inter-regional river connectivity to facilitate trade, commerce and tourism.",""],[1,"212","13","Integrated Inland Water Transport with Other Transport Modes","Integrate IWT with other transport modes to maximize the benefits of IWT.",""],[1,"212","14","River Transport Safety Standards Improvement","Sharply improve river transport safety standards by setting proper standards and ensuring full compliance.",""],[1,"212","15","Vessel Worthiness Licensing System","Vessel worthiness licensing would ensure minimum service facilities and standards of all vessels.",""],[1,"212","16","BIWTA Institutional Strengthening for Licensing Administration","Bangladesh Inland Water Transport Authority (BIWTA) will be strengthened with technical staff and qualified inspectors to administer all licensing functions efficiently and on time.",""],[1,"212","17","BIWTA Hydrological Survey and River Training Capacity Expansion","The capacity of BIWTA to undertake hydrological surveys, conduct river training and implement dredging operations will be expanded through upgrading the managerial and technical staff and international training.",""],[1,"212","17","Public-Private Partnership for River Operations","Side by side, the private sector will be invited to participate in these operations on a PPP basis.",""],[1,"213","2","Riverport Facilities Modernization Programme","Riverport facilities will be sharply improved with modern service standards for passengers, docking and unloading services for cargo including container cargo, storage facilities and security and rescue services.",""],[1,"213","2","Customs and Inspection Services at International River Ports","International river ports of call will also provide customs and inspection services as relevant.",""],[1,"213","3","Commercially Determined Passenger and Cargo Pricing Policy","Pricing policies for passenger and cargo will be commercially determined with a view to enabling a reasonable rate of return on investment.",""]],"9":[[1,"24","2","Urban Mass Transit and Metro Rail Network Development","The Transport Sector Strategy for PP2041: will focus on: (iv) Introducing a time saving electrical Urban Mass Transit / Metro Rail Network to reduce urban traffic congestion and improve the natural environment;",""]],"10":[[1,"134","6","Railway Modernization and High-Speed Train Network Development","Investment in modernization and establishment of speed train network have to be on cards.",""],[1,"210","9","Strategic Railway Modernization and Upgrading Process","A strategic railway modernization and upgrading process would be institutionalized taking a forward view over the next 20 years.",""],[1,"210","9","Multi-Year Railway Investment Plan","It shall comprise a multi- year investment plan fully supported by a credible funding plan.",""],[1,"211","2","Rail Supply Augmentation","Augmentation of supply (more trains and longer trains) to ensure full satisfaction of demand for both passenger and freight.",""],[1,"211","3","Railway Infrastructure Expansion and Upgrading Programme","Expand and strengthen railway infrastructure including creating new lines to service demand, track doubling of important corridors, upgradation of all rail lines to broad gauge/ dual gauge system.",""],[1,"211","5","Modern Railway Signalling and Telecommunications Upgrade","Introduction and/or upgradation of modern signalling system with relevant safety measures of international standard and introduction of a proper telecommunication system.",""],[1,"211","6","Mechanized Track Maintenance System","Introduction of mechanized track maintenance system.",""],[1,"211","7","Operations and Maintenance Safety Standards Strengthening","Strengthen O&M practices following internationally recognized safety standards.",""],[1,"211","9","Port Freight Train Turnaround Time Reduction","Reduction of turnaround time for the port bound freight trains.",""],[1,"211","10","Modern Train Management System with Centralized Traffic Control","Introduction of a modern train management system with the Centralized Traffic Control System.",""],[1,"211","11","Station Redevelopment and Passenger Facility Improvement","Redevelopment of stations for smooth flow and comfortable experience of passengers as also with ensuring cleanliness and hygienic environment.",""],[1,"211","13","Railway Human Resources Upgradation for Service Commercialization","Upgradation of railway human resources aimed at commercializing services.",""],[1,"211","14","Coach Redesign for Passenger Comfort and Safety","Redesign of coaches to enhance travel comfort and safety.",""],[1,"211","18","Demand-Based New Train Service Expansion","Increase new train service based on demand.",""],[1,"211","19","Development of New Inland Container Depots","Development of new Inland Container Depots.",""],[1,"211","20","National Railway Connectivity Expansion","Ensure railway connectivity to every district of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"211","21","Railway Missing Links Reconstruction and Modernization Programme","Reconstruction, modernization and extension of missing links for national, regional and Trans Asian Railway Network.",""],[1,"211","22","Dedicated Freight Corridor Development","Development of dedicated freight corridors.",""],[1,"211","23","Commuter Train Services Introduction","Introduction of Commuter Train Services for reducing traffic jam in megacities.",""],[1,"211","24","Electric Traction Introduction for Bangladesh Railway","Introduction of electric traction in Bangladesh Railway.",""],[1,"211","25","Workshop Development and Rolling Stock Maintenance Equipment Procurement","Development of new Workshops.",""],[1,"212","1","Intermediate Block System and Automatic Train Supervision Installation","Introduction of Intermediate Block System and Installation of Automatic Train Supervision (ATS) including Automatic Train Protection (ATP) with existing CBI and CTC system in the selected corridors.",""],[1,"212","2","Railway Zonal and Divisional Expansion","Creation of two additional zones and four additional divisions in Railway for better and effective management of railway services.",""],[1,"212","3","Railway Link Development to Ports and Deep Sea Port","Development of railway links with all ports and proposed Deep Sea Port at Sonadia.",""],[1,"212","4","Improved Customs Clearance Arrangements for Inter-Regional Services","Improved custom clearance arrangements for inter-regional services with neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"212","5","Road Transport Transfer Facilities Improvement","Quality transfer facilities to road transport.",""],[1,"212","6","Business Planning to Expand Passenger and Freight Market Share","Strengthen business planning to capture a higher market share of passenger and freight traffic including special services for tourist and high-end users.",""],[1,"212","7","Railway Training Academy Upgradation and Construction","Upgradation/construction of railway training academy.",""],[1,"212","8","Bangladesh Railway Multimodal Transport Operator Role","Bangladesh Railway to act as a multi-modal transport operator.",""]],"11":[[1,"205","2","MRT Line-6 Completion","The targeted completion of MRT Line-6 (the first elevated Metro Rail of Bangladesh) has been set for December 2021.",""],[1,"205","2","Construction of Three Additional MRT Lines","Substantial progress of construction works of three more MRT Lines (Line-1; Line-5 North; and Line-5 South) are expected within PP2021.",""],[1,"205","2","Transport User Charges and Private Participation Reform","Efforts were also to be made to improve resource mobilization through the introduction of user charges and fees and promote greater private sector participation in transport services infrastructure building.",""],[1,"206","3","Trade Logistics and Transport Efficiency Improvement","These implementation and policy constraints will be addressed comprehensively under PP2041.",""],[1,"207","2","Intermodal Transport System Transformation","For domestic travel, the balance of transport services changes in favour of rail and inland water and away from the excessive reliance on the road network.",""],[1,"207","2","Port and Air Transport Capacity Expansion","Port and air traffic capacities are projected to grow rapidly to meet the growing demand from higher GDP growth.",""],[1,"207","2","Mass Rapid Transit and Metro Rail Network Expansion","Urban transport changes are particularly dramatic as mass rapid transit (MRT)/Metro Rail Network transit options are introduced initially in the capital city of Dhaka and adjoining areas but then expanded to all major cities.",""],[1,"207","8","Transport Strategy Implementation Gap Remediation","An important priority will be to address the implementation gaps of the PP2021 strategy.",""],[1,"207","8","Transport Project Institutional Constraint Reform","The other priority will be to address the major institutional constraints that have hampered implementation of transport projects.",""],[1,"207","8","PPP Strategy Reform for Transport Delivery","A third priority is the reform of the PPP strategy with a view to achieving stronger progress under PP2041.",""],[1,"208","1","Transformational Transport Infrastructure Investment Prioritization","Bangladesh needs to be more strategic about identifying major transport projects and then allocating resources accordingly.",""],[1,"208","2","Transport Sector Master Plan 2041 Development","a fresh look will be taken to develop a long-term Transport Sector Master Plan 2041 (TSMP 2041) with international technical assistance",""],[1,"208","3","Balanced Intermodal Transport Development","PP2041 will give priority to developing these modes to reduce the pressure on roads and also to strengthen inter- modal coordination.",""],[1,"208","3","Integrated Transport Planning Process","These and other options to improve the intermodal transport balance will be adopted based on an integrated transport planning process that will be regularly updated to reflect the changing traffic dynamics.",""],[1,"208","4","Transport Project Implementation Capacity Strengthening","PP2041 will further strengthen this by closely monitoring completion of all large transport projects, ensuring timely release of funds, linking new investment approvals to the record of project implementation, improving procurement policies, paying greater attention to project design before project approval, ensuring project implementation readiness as an important criteria for project approval, and strengthening capacities of line ministries and public agencies through improvement in technical capacities based on training and also through recruitment of special skills from private sector on contractual basis.","line ministries | public agencies"],[1,"208","5","Transport Infrastructure Financing and Implementation Strengthening","PP2041 will assign priority to strengthening implementation",""],[1,"209","1","Strengthening the Public-Private Partnership Initiative for Transport Infrastructure Financing","To achieve sustainable financing of this large transport infrastructure programme, the PP2041 will seek to sharply strengthen the PPP initiative with quality international level staffs and address required legal and incentive issues to draw international financing from best possible sources.",""],[1,"213","1","Public-Private Balance in Infrastructure and Transport Service Provision","Given the large need for resources, a proper balance between the public and private sector will be maintained.",""]],"12":[[1,"24","1","Trade Logistics Improvement for Factory-Port Movements","The acceleration in growth under PP2041 and the diversification of the export basket will require strong improvements in trade logistics related to factory to port movements and timely inflow of imports of capital machinery and intermediate imports from ports to factory gate.",""],[1,"24","1","PP2021 Transport Strategy Implementation Gap Closure","An important priority will be to address the implementation gaps of the PP2021 strategy.",""],[1,"24","1","Transport Project Institutional Constraint Reform","The other priority will be to address the major institutional constraints that have hampered implementation of transport projects.",""],[1,"24","1","Public-Private Partnership Strategy Reform","A third priority is the reform of the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) strategy with a view to achieving stronger progress under PP2041.",""],[1,"24","1","Strategic Prioritization of Major Transport Projects","Bangladesh needs to be more strategic about identifying major transport projects and then allocating resources accordingly.",""],[1,"24","2","Transport Sector Long-Term Planning and Priority Setting","The Transport Sector Strategy for PP2041: will focus on: (i) Strengthening long-term planning and priority setting;",""],[1,"24","2","Inter-Modal Transport Balance Improvement","The Transport Sector Strategy for PP2041: will focus on: (ii) Improving inter-modal transport balance;",""],[1,"24","2","Transport Implementation Capacity Strengthening","The Transport Sector Strategy for PP2041: will focus on: (iii) Strengthening implementation capacity;",""],[1,"24","2","Sustainable Transport Infrastructure Financing","The Transport Sector Strategy for PP2041: will focus on: (v) Ensuring sustainable financing of transport infrastructure;",""],[1,"24","2","Transport Service Quality and Reliability Policy Development","The Transport Sector Strategy for PP2041: will focus on: (vi) Developing and implementing key policies for ensuring quality and reliability of transport services;",""],[1,"24","2","Public Transport Authority Management Capacity Strengthening","The Transport Sector Strategy for PP2041: will focus on: (vii) Strengthening management capabilities and efficiency of public transport authorities;",""],[1,"24","2","Modern Transport Facilities Implementation and Operation","The Transport Sector Strategy for PP2041: will focus on: (viii) Implementing and operating modern transport facilities in line with the traffic needs of 2041.",""],[1,"65","7","Infrastructure Investment Mobilization","There will be massive increases in infrastructure investment which cannot be met entirely from domestic resources, so the government will have to reach out for various multilateral or bilateral sources besides inviting public-private partnerships, both local and foreign.",""],[1,"70","3","Public-Private Partnership Delivery of Large Infrastructure Projects","In addition to relying on ADP resources, the Government will go for Public-Private Partnership arrangements in delivering large infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"78","1","Public Infrastructure Investment Expansion","Additional public investments in infrastructure improvements will be necessary.",""],[1,"82","2","Padma Bridge Construction","The construction of the Bangabandhu Bridge and the ongoing Padma Bridge are important examples of this.",""],[1,"82","2","Inter-City Transport Connectivity Upgrades","Additionally, inter-city air transport and road connections have been strengthened.",""],[1,"82","2","Inland Water Transport and Highway Upgrading","The PP2041 will further strengthen this effort with additional emphasis on inland water transport and upgrading of inter-city highways.",""]],"13":[[1,"110","1","Waterway Re-excavation and Transport Improvement","attention should be given to improve waterways by re-excavation of rivers and canals.",""],[1,"110","1","Rail Transport Expansion and Upgrading for Agricultural Freight","The rail transport facilities fall far short of requirement and need to be expanded and improved for transporting agricultural products at a cheaper rate.",""],[1,"110","4","Rural Roads and Road Infrastructure Maintenance","The Road Users Cost (RUC) will be maintained at minimum as possible by maintaining the rural roads and road infrastructures to keep the transportation cost of farm product at affordable level.",""],[1,"119","4","Climate-Resilient Core Road Network Development","Climate resilient core road network development up-to every village supportive to accommodate high middle income economy will be given priority.",""],[1,"119","8","My Village- My Town Community Spaces and Recreation Facilities Development","Local Government Engineering Department under Local Government Division will develop community spaces and recreation facilities in the villages under their 'My Village- My Town' programs.","Local Government Division"],[1,"119","9","Rural Infrastructure Development with Support Services","Rural infrastructure development with support services will be given high priority in order to create a positive environment for rural job creation;",""],[1,"120","9","Village Connectivity to Upazila Headquarters","All villages will be connected with Upazila headquarters;",""],[1,"120","11","Expansion and Upgrading of Rural Growth Centers","it is imperative to increase the number of growth centers throughout the country and use them innovatively for employment creation and overall growth of the rural economy.",""]],"14":[[1,"209","2","Road Maintenance Financing from User Charges","These resources will be used to improve the maintenance of roads, bridges and highways.",""],[1,"210","2","National Highway Network Upgrading and Access-Control Expressway Development","Consolidating and upgrading National Highway Networks through multi-laning of existing highways, by establishing access-control long-distance expressways, and by creating service lanes to ease connectivity to local roads.",""],[1,"210","2","Strict Axle Load Control Enforcement","Strict axle load control policy would be established and enforced to reduce road damages caused by overloading.",""],[1,"210","2","High-Speed Highway Corridor Development","The focus will be given to developing quality infrastructures with hallmark attribute of high-speed mobility facilities.",""],[1,"210","2","Town Bypass Access-Control Expressway Program","Bypasses around towns would be planned and provided as access-controlled expressway type facilities with entry/exit at predetermined locations.",""],[1,"210","3","Inter-Regional Connectivity Infrastructure Linkage Programme","Establishing connectivity with inter-regional highways, economic zone areas, ports, airports, power stations, inland water transport facilities, rail stations and rail freight centres and major tourist resorts to maximize the benefits of the highways system.",""],[1,"210","4","Inter-District Road and Bridge Upgrading Programme","Ensuring inter-district connectivity for all districts that are not connected through the national highway system.",""],[1,"210","5","Highway and Inter-District Traveler Service Facilities","Creating highway and inter-district facilities to provide restroom and food facilities for travellers and essential services such as gas stations, emergency repairs, for facilitating highway mobility.",""],[1,"210","6","Zilla and Upazilla Road Upgrading Programme","Upgrading of all zilla and upazilla roads to facilitate easy transport connectivity between production and consumption centres.",""],[1,"210","7","Village Road Asphalt Upgrading Programme","All village roads would be converted to asphalt standard with at least one lane to facilitate rural mobility of passengers and products.",""],[1,"210","8","Road User Charges and Toll Financing for Road Maintenance","The development and implementation of a well-designed road user charges will be instrumental in providing resources for road upgrading and maintenance.",""]],"15":[[1,"134","5","Dhaka-Chattogram 8-Lane Highway Upgrade","This road needs to be converted into an 8-lane highway along with all the trappings of modern traffic management.",""]],"16":[[1,"214","4","Port Productivity Modernization Programme","Each port would focus on the improvement of productivity both ship berth-day and gang- shift output further through modernisation, induction of more sophisticated equipment in handling cargo, etc.",""],[1,"214","5","Outsourcing and Privatization of Handling Operations","Handling operations in selected areas will gradually be outsourced/privatised for injecting more competition and increasing output.",""],[1,"214","6","Cargo Handling Mechanization in Major Ports","Efforts would be made for full mechanization of cargo handling operation and movement in major Ports.",""],[1,"214","7","Port Storage Area Expansion","The storage area in the ports will be expanded.",""],[1,"214","8","Port Vessel Turnaround Time Improvement","Efforts would be made to reduce pre-berthing detention and to improve turn -time of vessels through minimization of both port and non-port related factors.",""],[1,"214","9","Required Dredging for Larger Shipping Capacity","Required dredging to allow handling of bigger shipping will be carried out.",""],[1,"214","10","Terminal Cargo Handling Capacity Expansion","Terminal capacity for handling higher cargo off-loading will be expanded.",""],[1,"214","11","Deep-Water Container Hub Port Construction","Capacity to handle large container traffic will be expanded by constructing deep water- container hub ports.",""],[1,"214","12","Inter-modal Port Connectivity Improvement","Inter-modal transport connectivity with ports will be ensured for speedy forward transport to the final destination of imports as well as easy transit factory gate to port for exports.",""],[1,"214","13","Modern Cargo Handling Techniques for Major Ports","Modern cargo handling techniques would be introduced to improve port performance in the major ports, particularly in the dry bulk cargo, conventional and unitized general cargo trades.",""],[1,"214","14","Integrated Port Operations System and Port Automation","Port service efficiency and productivity will be enhanced by introducing of state-of-the-art technology/internet to implement integrated Port Operations System and to move towards paperless regime so as to reduce dwell time and also reduce transaction cost to the users.",""],[1,"236","1","Blue Economy Development Initiative","PP2021 also sought to exploit the benefits of the blue economy with the focus on the shipping industry, port services and marine fishing.",""]],"17":[[1,"17","3","Delta Plan 2100 Implementation","The government has already adopted the Delta Plan and the implementation is underway.",""],[1,"25","4","Delta Plan Implementation for Climate Resilience","The specific strategies, policies and institutional reforms include: (b) Implementing the Delta Plan to Build Resilience and Reduce Vulnerability to Climate Change;",""],[1,"82","3","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100","The government has adopted a major long-term initiative called the Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 (BDP2100) that seeks to improve the management of water, land, ecology, environment and climate change through strategies, policies, investment programmes and institutions.",""],[1,"82","3","Flood Control and Water Management Strategy Package","The associated strategies for flood control, water storage, irrigation, land management, agriculture, forestry resource management, and ecological balance will be major elements of the policy package for reducing poverty and improving environmental management during PP2041.",""],[1,"237","3","Long-Term Water Management Investments","the government's attention has to shift to better management of the environmental and climate change risks by taking long term investments in water management.",""],[1,"239","4","Polder Management Improvement Programme","Some of the important investment programmes include: sharply improved polder management;",""],[1,"239","4","Flood Control Programmes in Haor Areas","a range of flood control programmes including in the haor areas;",""],[1,"239","4","Major River Barrage and Restoration Projects","Ganges Barrage Project; Brahmaputra Barrage Project, the Gorai River Restoration Project; River Dredging and River Training projects;",""],[1,"239","4","Ecological Restoration of Major Lakes","and projects to restore the ecological balance of major lakes (major haor, baor and jheels).",""],[1,"239","5","Increase Public Spending on Water Resources","Important policy reforms consist of increasing public spending on water resources from 0.8% of GDP now to 2% of GDP by FY2020;",""],[1,"239","5","Increase Water Sector Operations and Maintenance Spending","increasing O&M spending from a negligible amount now to at least 0.5% of GDP by FY2020;",""],[1,"239","5","Promote Public-Private Partnerships in Water Services","provide incentives to encourage public-private partnerships (PPP) in water supply, water transport, river dredging and sanitation;",""],[1,"239","5","Strengthen Water Sharing Dialogue with India","strengthen dialogue with India on better and more equitable sharing of upstream water including joint projects that yield multiple benefits so that water sharing is not a zero-sum game.",""],[1,"239","6","Delta Governance and Financing Framework","Major institutional reforms include: establishment of the Delta Act, the Delta Wing and the Delta Fund that will provide the institutional framework for holistic planning, budgeting, project selection, research and monitoring and evaluation of water and water-related projects;",""],[1,"239","6","Local Water User Associations for Project Implementation","and the establishment of the water user associations (WUA) at the local level that will have primary responsibility for implementing all local-level water projects including O&M.",""],[1,"239","6","Beneficiary-Pays Principle for Local Water Projects","The government will introduce beneficiary-pays-principle for all local water projects and O&M so that over time the water resource and related hazard management become largely beneficiary managed and financed and therefore fully sustainable.",""]],"18":[[1,"103","5","Groundwater Use Reduction and Water Use Efficiency Improvement","In order to reduce groundwater use, we need to increase water use efficiency in crop production and enhance the utilization of surface",""],[1,"104","1","Non-Rice Crop Diversification for Boro Season","In order to minimize groundwater use, cultivation of non- rice crops particularly maize and mung bean may be encouraged during boro season.",""],[1,"104","1","Improved Irrigation Efficiency and Smart Irrigation Introduction","Increased irrigation efficiency instead of flood irrigation, localized irrigation method such as smart and sensor-based irrigation will be introduced among farmers, especially for horticultural crop production.",""],[1,"108","5","Precision Irrigation and Water Management Systems","the challenge will be to have in place sound water management systems that not only help preserve surface water through rainwater harvesting, building of reservoirs to hold such water, and also reducing the wastage of",""],[1,"109","1","ICT-Enabled Irrigation Water Management","Use of ICT along with digital solutions to irrigation water management could be one of the ways of mitigating this challenge and also achieving sustainable water availability for irrigation in the coming decades.",""],[1,"109","2","Drip Irrigation Innovation Incentive Policies","So there needs to be policies that could incentivize innovations in drip irrigation.",""],[1,"109","2","Smart Irrigation Technology Deployment","There are now technologically advanced systems, which get linked to the Internet via the cloud and are automated, driven by sensors that determine the appropriate amount of water needed at specific crop sites.",""],[1,"109","2","Crop Water Requirement and Irrigation Scheduling Reform","Water requirement of crops and irrigation scheduling will properly be addressed in order to increase water use efficiency and decrease the loss of precious water resources in future.",""],[1,"115","2","Well-Planned Irrigation Management System","Therefore, a well-planned irrigation management system is essential for a gradual increase of cropping intensity as well as yield.",""],[1,"115","2","Modern Water Management Technology Promotion","Irrigation efficiency will be ascertained and modern water management technology will be promoted to enhance irrigation efficacy and water productivity through optimal use of available water resources.",""],[1,"115","2","Rainwater Harvesting and Small-Scale Water Resources Development","As part of the strategy water reservoir/rainwater harvesting in rainfed/coastal/hilly areas will have to be encouraged, and small scale water resources systems could be developed (particularly through LGED/WDB/BMDC/BMDA) along with monitoring the maintenance of the small scale water resources infrastructure at local levels by water management groups/cooperative associationsand taking care of environmental and social issues.",""],[1,"118","1","Water Harvesting, Retention, and Efficient Irrigation Improvement","Improving water harvesting and retention (through the use of pools, dams, pits, retaining ridges, increasing soil organic matter to heighten the water retention capacity of soils) and water-use efficiency (irrigation systems).",""],[1,"121","2","Efficient Irrigation Systems","efficient irrigation systems",""],[1,"121","3","Integrated Water Management Scale-Up","the priority is to scale up existing good practices of water conservation and management and apply more widely integrated water management",""],[1,"121","3","Flood Control and Early Warning Measures","including flood control and prevention schemes, flood early warning systems",""],[1,"121","3","Irrigation Improvement and Demand-Side Water Management","irrigation improvement, and demand-side management",""]],"19":[[1,"119","6","Rural Safe Water Supply Expansion","Availability of safe water will be a top priority in all villages with special attention to salinity prone coastal areas, arsenic prone areas, hilly, haor and char areas.",""],[1,"119","6","Piped and Mini-Piped Water Supply Expansion","There will be gradual increase of piped and mini piped water supply in densly populated villages throughout the country.",""],[1,"119","6","Rural Sanitation and Fecal Sludge Management Improvement","special effort will be given in sanitation and fecal sludge management for restoration of aquative environment of the rural areas.",""],[1,"119","7","Rural Waste Management Model Development","Effective Waste Management Model will be developed for Rural Growth Centres/Markets and as well as villages.",""],[1,"119","7","Local Government Waste Management Capacity Building","Capacity of LGIs will be enhanced to deal with waste management at rural level.",""]],"20":[[1,"240","5","Surface Water Pollution Prevention and Clean-Up Drive","In addition to laws and regulations that set preventive measures, the polluter pays principle will be applied to create a strong disincentive against illegal disposal of industrial, commercial and household wastes in surface water bodies.",""],[1,"240","5","Surface Water Clean-Up and Wastewater Treatment Arrangements","At the same time, urgent actions will be taken to launch surface water clean-up drive including arrangements to treat drainage/sewerage water before it reaches public water bodies.",""],[1,"240","5","National Campaigns for Community Water Pollution Awareness","Community education and participation will be ensured through national campaigns using print and video media and in partnership with NGOs.",""],[1,"240","6","Groundwater Sustainability and Governance Measures","During the implementation of this plan, the pertinent issue of groundwater sustainability will be addressed with the definite objectives of groundwater protection from depletion, contamination, protection of groundwater dependent ecosystems, optimum use of groundwater and its governance.",""],[1,"244","1","Water and Sewerage Cost Recovery Pricing Reform","This pricing policy would be changed, both to mobilize funding for new investments as well as to ensure efficient use of water.",""]],"21":[[1,"236","1","Environmental Degradation and Climate Change Response Framework","the PP2021 sought to initiate a comprehensive long-term approach to address environmental degradation and climate change through a mixture of laws, regulations, policies and programmes.",""],[1,"236","3","Environmental Law and Climate Adaptation Implementation","Many laws and regulations have been enacted over the years to protect the environment and programmes and policies are in place to adapt and mitigate the adverse effects of climate change.",""],[1,"236","3","Air and Water Pollution Control Measures","This progress continued under the 6th FYP, with special emphasis on air and water pollution control.",""],[1,"236","3","Brick Kiln Air Pollution Management","the focus on implementation was strengthened with significant progress in managing the air pollution from brick kilns",""],[1,"236","3","Leather Industry Water Pollution Reduction","and reducing water pollution from the leather industry.",""],[1,"238","4","Environmental Governance Incentives and Regulatory Policy Framework","Environmental governance is such whereby there is a sound mix of incentives and regulatory policies including the application of the polluter pays principle and a decentralized implementation of environmental policies and programmes.",""],[1,"239","2","Integration of Environmental Protection into Macroeconomic Framework","the growth strategy would recognize environmental protection as an integral part of the macroeconomic framework",""],[1,"240","1","Polluter Pays Fiscal Policy for Environmental Management","Bangladesh will adopt two major principles in the conduct of fiscal policy for better environmental management: (1) beneficiary pays principle; and (2) polluter pays principle.",""]],"22":[[1,"237","1","National Low-Carbon Mitigation Action","Bangladesh has expressed her intention in the NDC (Nationally Determined Contributions) to take action on mitigation in order to reduce GHGs emissions by following a low carbon development pathway.",""],[1,"237","2","National Adaptation Plan Roadmap and NAP Formulation","Bangladesh has prepared a NAP Roadmap towards formulating a comprehensive National Adaptation Plan (NAP) with a view to reducing vulnerability to the impacts of climate change by building adaptive capacity and resilience.",""],[1,"237","2","Climate Adaptation Integration into Policies and Development Planning","the NAP will also facilitate the integration of climate change adaptation, into relevant new and existing policies, programmes and activities in a coherent manner, in particular, development planning processes and strategies, within all relevant sectors and at different levels, as appropriate.",""],[1,"237","2","Bangladesh Climate Change Strategy and Action Plan Update","Bangladesh is also under the process of updating the BCCSAP.",""],[1,"239","1","Green Growth Strategy","under PP2041 Bangladesh will adopt a green growth strategy.",""],[1,"239","3","Delta Plan 2100 Implementation","One of the highest priorities is to reduce the vulnerability of the population to natural hazards and climate change by implementing the Delta plan 2100 (BDP2100).",""],[1,"239","3","Climate Vulnerability Reduction Policies, Investments, and Institutional Reforms","The BDP2100 includes major policies, investment programmes and institutional reforms that if adopted and implemented properly will address the sources of long-term climate change vulnerability at source thereby building resilience and reducing the adverse effects of climate change on the population.",""]],"23":[[1,"241","1","Dhaka Solid Waste Management Master Plan","Dhaka City Corporation has a master plan underway to better handle solid waste management.",""],[1,"241","1","Expanded Waste Management Initiatives","During the implementation of PP2041, the country intends to add more initiatives with the current ones with more impetus.",""]],"24":[[1,"17","3","Public-Private Reforestation and Afforestation Partnerships","In the forestry sector, the priority is to implement effective public-private partnerships for reforestation and afforestation.",""],[1,"84","1","Hill Region Forest and Biodiversity Protection Measures","Steps will also be taken to increase the coverage of forest in the hill region and to protect the environment, and biodiversity.",""]],"25":[[1,"236","3","Biodiversity Improvement Measures","Important steps were also taken to improve biodiversity.",""]],"26":[[1,"241","2","Gorai River Restoration","A particularly important step is the restoration of the Gorai River that will restore the supply of freshwater to the Sundarbans and clean out the intrusion of saline water.",""],[1,"241","2","Oil Spill and Shipping Waste Pollution Control","Another important step will be to manage oil spillovers from shipping and dumping of shipping scraps in the Bay of Bengal area.",""],[1,"241","2","Sundarbans SMART Monitoring and Reporting","To protect the Sundarbans from oil spill pollution as well as noise pollution and to reduce the risk of wildlife poaching Special Monitoring and Reporting Tools (SMART) will be continued all over the Sundarbans.",""],[1,"241","2","Ecological Corridor Establishment","Ecological corridors will be established to maintain adequate space for viable populations of wild species in all protected areas by implementing a stepwise approach through corridor modelling.",""],[1,"241","2","Protected Area Resettlement and Encroachment Reduction Plan","Habitat fragmentation and encroachment will be reduced by decreasing human occupations inside the protected areas through resettlement.",""],[1,"241","2","Resettlement Action Plan for Protected Areas","a resettlement action plan elaborating all required conditions and measures will be prepared.",""],[1,"241","3","Forest Department Staffing and Capacity Strengthening","Forest Department will be strengthened by recruiting sufficient manpower to protect forest land and forest resources.","Forest Department"],[1,"241","3","Forest Law Penalty Reform and Enforcement","To protect forest land and forest resources, the penalty provision of existing laws may be amended to enhance their rigour and enforced strictly so that forest offenders get scared to commit any offence.",""],[1,"241","3","Community Co-management of Forest Resources","The forest-dependent local people will be involved directly at large scale in forest management through co-management.",""],[1,"241","3","Tree Plantation on Government Forest and Marginal Lands","The government forest land of Chittagong Hill Tracts will be taken under tree cover through different types of plantation activities with suitable plantation module.",""],[1,"241","3","Alternative Livelihood Support for Forest-Dependent Poor","Along with strategies to promote alternative livelihood opportunities for the forest-dependent poor in partnership with community-based groups and NGOS, the capacity of the Forest Department will be sharply strengthened to regularly update the forestry database and implement all forest and wildlife preservation acts, rules, and guidelines.","Forest Department"],[1,"241","3","Factory-Gate Logging Tax","Consideration will be given to imposing a logging tax administered at the factory gate.",""],[1,"241","3","Ban on Harvesting Forest Produce from Natural Forests","Banning on harvesting on forest produce from the natural forest will be continued.",""],[1,"241","3","Strict Penalties for Illegal Tree Felling","Strict penalties will be imposed on illegal tree felling and all forest-related illegal activities.",""],[1,"242","1","Bangladesh National REDD+ Strategy Implementation","The Bangladesh National REDD+ Strategy (2016-2031), a detailed forest sectoral strategy, is laying out policies and measures to reduce emission from deforestation and forest degradation and to increase forest carbon stock in the country.",""],[1,"246","1","Ecologically Critical Areas Enforcement and Coastal Habitat Conservation","In the environment sector, several Ecologically Critical Areas (ECA) have been enforced in various coastal ecosystems to maintain critical habitats, biodiversity, marine turtle breeding and conservation, and mangrove restoration and growth.",""],[1,"246","1","Mangrove Afforestation in Newly Accreted Intertidal Areas","Mangrove afforestation in newly accreted intertidal areas is going on for decades now.",""],[1,"247","4","Marine and Coastal Ecosystem Restoration and Sustainable Management","by 2020, start the restoration process for degraded marine and coastal ecosystems in appropriate cases, i.e. Chakaria Sundarban and establish sustainable management",""],[1,"247","7","Marine Protected Areas Establishment","Several steps will be taken including: establish marine protected areas (MPAs) - one declared around 'Swatch of No Ground';",""],[1,"247","7","Waste Minimization Measures for Fisheries","promote efficient waste minimization measures and techniques, and strengthen research and study.",""]],"27":[[1,"15","2","Expanded Human Capital Investment for the Poor","Adequate investment in human capital formation of the poor is perhaps the most pressing policy challenge facing Bangladesh in the coming years.",""],[1,"15","2","Microcredit Expansion and Financial Access Support","The PP2041 strategy will further build on this positive experience.",""],[1,"66","1","Financial System Reform for Rural and Small Saver Access","reforms in the financial system to provide easy access of rural population and small savers to formal financial institutions",""],[1,"66","1","Digital Financial Inclusion Expansion","ensuring greater financial inclusion through mobile and digital technology",""],[1,"76","3","Poverty Reduction Strategy to Reverse Income Inequality","the pattern of rising income inequality and associated underlying inequalities in access to human and physical capital will have to be arrested and reversed in the PP2041 Poverty Reduction Strategy to strengthen the fight against poverty.",""],[1,"77","2","Expanded Access to Education and Health Services for the Poor","Stronger efforts are needed to improve the access of the poor to better education and health services.",""],[1,"77","2","Human Capital Formation for Poverty Reduction","Improved human capital formation will assume a bigger role as Bangladesh transforms towards a higher income economy.",""],[1,"77","3","Continued Microcredit Support","Continued focus on microcredit will be important for further reducing extreme poverty.",""],[1,"77","3","Expanded Access to Institutional Credit","At the same time, greater access to institutional credit will support the buildup of human and physical capital for the poor.",""],[1,"81","1","Microcredit and Institutional Credit Expansion for the Poor","The objective would be to expand the scope and access to microcredit for the poor, reduce the cost of credit and improve the broader access of the poor to institutional credit.",""],[1,"81","1","Credit Market Improvement Measures","Steps will be taken to improve the credit market through a range of measures including credit bureaus, credit guarantee schemes, and a range FinTech initiatives.",""]],"28":[[1,"84","1","Ethnic Minority Rights and Empowerment Package","ethnic minorities by fulfilling their socio-economic, political and cultural rights, safeguarding their language and culture, fully implementing the CHT Accord 1997, ensuring access to education, health care services, employment, and protecting land rights.",""],[1,"84","1","Scaled-Up Investment for Ethnic Community Development","The ethnic communities will be empowered through scaled-up investment in health, nutrition, education, agricultural technologies, employment generation, ICT, expansion of microfinance, and social protection.",""]],"29":[[1,"84","1","Disability Rights Promotion and Mainstreaming","The government will undertake considerable measures to promote and protect the rights of persons with disabilities to facilitate their full participation in line with international and national commitments and policies.",""],[1,"84","1","Disability Mainstreaming in National Planning and Budgeting","The disability issue will be mainstreamed in the national planning process including budgetary system.",""]],"30":[[1,"90","12","Annual Youth Employment Guarantee from Each Upazila","Employment of 1000 youth (both male and female) should be ensured every year from each Upazila.",""],[1,"98","2","Youth Development and Future Generations Investment","The government has been devoted to the development of youth and plans to continue investing in their future in the upcoming decades, so as to pave the way to achieving the development goals and commitments at the national level and the international level such as Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).",""],[1,"104","4","Rural Technology Centres and Business Services Expansion","In line with \"Amar Gram Amar Shohor\" of the government, technological services will be expanded at the communities by establishing Rural Technology Centres and business services in strategic locations of rural Bangladesh.",""],[1,"119","10","Rural Agro-based Small Industry Promotion","Agro-based small industries will be encouraged in rural areas",""],[1,"119","10","Business-Friendly Rural Commerce Environment","congenial atmosphere for business and commerce should be ensured to create employment opportunities for youths, especially higher educated ones who will be the human capital resources of the future",""],[1,"120","2","Rural Law and Order Improvement","Improvement of rural law and order will be ensured,",""],[1,"120","3","Small and Medium Entrepreneurship Support Programs","There will be programs to encourage and support small and medium entrepreneurship,",""],[1,"120","4","Rural Investment Promotion for Employment Creation","Foreign and local investment in rural areas will be encouraged to create employment opportunities,",""],[1,"120","5","Bank Credit Access Improvement","Access to bank credit will be improved;",""],[1,"157","4","Long-Term Employment Strategy for Employment-Intensive Growth","A long-term strategy for employment-intensive growth will consist of the following components:",""],[1,"158","4","Institutional Arrangement for Employment Services","But that arrangement has to be put in place now.",""],[1,"158","6","Informal Sector Job Quality and Social Protection Measures","And work in that direction has to be initiated now.",""],[1,"159","2","District Recruiting Agent and Employment Office Network","Recruiting agent and District Employment & Manpower Office (DEMO) will be introduced in each district of Bangladesh, with priority assigned to lagging districts.",""],[1,"161","10","Integrated Employment Strategy","there has to be an integrated approach to employment generation over the two decades of the Perspective Plan.",""],[1,"161","10","Employment-Oriented Macroeconomic Policy Framework","The starting off point for such a policy has to be macroeconomic policies which would have to look beyond their conventional function of maintaining macroeconomic stability and give due consideration to what happens on the employment front.",""],[1,"161","10","Coordinated Monetary, Fiscal, Trade, Exchange Rate, and Industrial Policy Application","Coordinated application of monetary, fiscal, trade, exchange rate, and industrial policies then becomes critical for attaining high rates of economic and employment growth.",""]],"31":[[1,"227","9","Housing Market Reform","a rapid reform of the housing market is essential.",""],[1,"228","1","Land Market Reform and Digitization of Land Records","Land market reforms include digitization of land records, simplification of land transactions including registration and reduction of financial cost of land transfers.",""],[1,"228","1","Long-Term Mortgage Industry Development","support this by improving the functioning of the land market, helping develop the long-term mortgage industry, developing urban transport and a policy of tax/subsidy to encourage low-cost housing supply is imperative.",""],[1,"228","2","Housing Finance Program Development Study","The Bangladesh Bank will commission a study that looks at the international experience to facilitate this.","Bangladesh Bank"]],"32":[[1,"228","1","Low-Cost Housing Tax and Subsidy Policy","support this by improving the functioning of the land market, helping develop the long-term mortgage industry, developing urban transport and a policy of tax/subsidy to encourage low-cost housing supply is imperative.",""],[1,"228","1","Release of Government Land for Low-Cost Housing","The government will also help ease the housing constraint by releasing government-owned land for low-cost housing and relaxing space use restrictions for this type of housing.",""],[1,"228","1","Relaxation of Space Use Restrictions for Low-Cost Housing","The government will also help ease the housing constraint by releasing government-owned land for low-cost housing and relaxing space use restrictions for this type of housing.",""],[1,"228","3","Low-Cost Housing Incentive Package","Fiscal incentives like tax write off for interest payments, low taxation of capital gains from primary residence sale and capital/interest subsidies for low-cost housing are possible ways to spur home ownership.",""],[1,"228","3","Low-Cost Housing Innovation Support","Finally, policy attention would be given to creating incentives for the development of low-cost housing solutions using new technology and environment-friendly construction options.",""],[1,"228","3","Research Support for Climate-Resilient Low-Cost Housing","The government will support research in new design and technology for low-cost housing that is consistent with the natural climate and hazard risks.",""]],"33":[[1,"7","5","Digitalization of Public Services","In the last decade, the government took initiatives to make every service digital.",""],[1,"22","4","Digital Bangladesh Initiative","The Digital Bangladesh initiative includes: (i) Developing human resources ready for the 21st century, (ii) Connecting citizens in ways most meaningful to them, (iii) Taking services to citizens' doorsteps and (iv) Making the private sector and market more productive and competitive through the use of digital technology.",""],[1,"23","1","Enabling Digital Platforms and Infrastructure for Service Delivery","the government needs to gradually move away from direct service delivery and more towards creating enabling digital platforms and infrastructure that enables the private sector, civil society and academia to partner and meet citizen's needs for modern personalized services.",""],[1,"23","4","Payments Interoperability Initiative","Payments across different types of banking and non-banking financial institutions are completely seamless (payments interoperability)",""],[1,"23","6","Universal Citizen Identification System","All service providers and financial institutions unambiguously identify every citizen (unique IDs)",""],[1,"23","7","Service Delivery Simplification and Digitization Acceleration","All government agencies will accelerate simplification of service delivery and adoption of innovation and digitization through a structured, multi-stakeholder engagement process that can expedite procurement, capacity development, implementation, maintenance and upgrades.",""],[1,"23","8","Evidence-Driven Policymaking and Data Revolution Initiative","It will therefore be paramount to leverage the emerging data revolution to ensure evidence-driven policymaking to leapfrog progress, enable improvement of existing services and creation of new services.",""],[1,"55","2","E-Governance Development and Application Investment","allocating resources for the development and application of e-governance",""],[1,"184","1","Digital Bangladesh Initiative","The spread of ICT revolution has received particular emphasis based on the personal attention provided by the Honorable Prime Minister under her Digital Bangladesh Initiative.",""],[1,"184","6","Citizen-Centric E-Initiatives and Digital Public Services","Development interventions have resulted in a number of citizen-centric e-initiatives and services such as multimedia classroom and teacher-led education content development in public schools, mobile phone-based health service from Upazila Health Complex, mobile financial services, agricultural and other livelihood information and services (e-Tathyakosh) online through grassroots outlets.",""],[1,"184","8","Integrated Digital Government and Public Service Transformation Roadmap","ICT division is also working on the integrated digital Government and strategic roadmap development for transforming public services on the digital space.","ICT division"],[1,"185","1","a2i Digital Public Service Delivery Program","Under the a2i program, the government has ensured people's easy access to public services by setting up a national web portal covering 46,500 government offices and 5,875 Digital Centres.",""],[1,"185","1","Union Digital Centres Online Service Delivery","Even people from remote villages are getting various services online through the 4,571 Union Digital Centres.",""],[1,"185","3","e-Mutation Land Service","a2i introduced e-Mutation service to provide citizen responsive, hassle-free land service with the use of ICT in improving the operation of land administration.",""],[1,"185","4","Digital Service Design Lab for Government Service Digitization","ali's Digital Service Design Lab is a unique innovative methodology for the rapid digitization of the government services involving service recipients and service participants under the guidance of technical experts.",""],[1,"185","5","Empathy Training for Civil Servants","ali has initiated an innovative 'Empathy Training' with the purpose of empowering civil servants to place themselves in citizens' shoes and motivate them with a sense of purpose for driving unprecedented improvements in public service delivery.",""],[1,"185","7","National Digital Enterprise Architecture for E-Government Integration","World Summit on the Information Society (WSIS) award-winning Bangladesh's National Digital Enterprise Architecture (BNDA) has been developed for the integration of essential e-Government services like e-pension, land record management, etc.",""],[1,"185","7","Porichoy Digital Identity Verification Service","'Porichoy' has been developed to provide easy access to ID verification services as a foundation to a host of citizen-focused services.",""],[1,"188","1","Union Digital Service Centres","through union digital service centres, Bangladesh has been taking critical services to the doorsteps of rural Bangladesh seeding the possibility of reducing inequality between urban and rural populations by leveraging digital opportunities.",""],[1,"189","3","Digital Service Transformation and E-Services Expansion","It's envisioned that Bangladesh keeps increasingly transferring major services, delivered by both public and private sectors, over digital platform resulting in declining transaction cost.",""],[1,"193","7","Electronic Public Service Delivery and Digital Payments Expansion","Thus, it will also be important for government to also acquire the capability to enable radically better services for the public.",""],[1,"193","8","Integrated Service and Payments Delivery Platforms","Thus, it is not sufficient to merely unify these but ensure interoperability across all the camps through integrated service and payments delivery platforms.",""],[1,"193","13","Universal Unique Identification for Citizens","All service providers and financial institutions unambiguously identify every citizen (unique IDs)",""],[1,"194","3","Service Delivery Simplification and Digitization Acceleration","All government agencies may accelerate simplification of service delivery and adoption of innovation and digitization through a structured, multi-stakeholder engagement process that can expedite procurement, capacity development, implementation, maintenance and upgrades.",""],[1,"199","14","Digital Bangladesh Implementation","Articulation and implementation of digital Bangladesh",""]],"34":[[1,"185","1","Post-e-Centre Conversion and IT Training Programme","Since 2017, 8500 post offices have been converted into post-e-centres where IT training is being provided.",""],[1,"216","3","Postal Service Modernization","Postal services will continue to be modernized through faster transfers of mail with greater reliability of services.",""],[1,"216","3","Private Postal Partnerships with Global Carriers","Private services in partnership with global carriers will continue to be encouraged.",""],[1,"216","3","Digital Mail Tracking Modernization","Service modernization through the use of digital technology such as mail tracking will be strengthened.",""]],"35":[[1,"184","8","ICT Policy 2018","ICT Division has formulated 'ICT Policy 2018' focusing on digital security, leveraging of emerging technologies like IoT, Big Data, Robotics, and AI, ICT in education, skill development, employment, innovation, business promotion, and SDG targets by 2030.","ICT Division"],[1,"186","2","Cybersecurity Strengthening and Digital Trust Measures","The digital signature has been introduced, and Digital Security Agency has been established, and measures have been taken to uplift cyber security issues to facilitate as well as increase trust of the digitization of services.",""],[1,"186","2","Government E-mail Policy 2018","Government e-mail Policy 2018",""],[1,"190","14","Digital Transformation and Enabling Platforms Strategy","Government needs to focus on: (1) Access and adoption, (2) Responsible digital transformation, (3) Fit for purpose, informed governance, (4) Secured and resilient people, processes and practices, (5) User-centric, interoperable digital identities, and (6) Trustworthy data innovation.",""],[1,"194","2","Citizen-Centric Technology Regulation","Alarming phenomenon such as the proliferation of fake news and control of personal data by mega corporations have to be addressed with citizen-centric regulation and mass digital literacy.",""],[1,"216","2","Information Integrity and Public Interest Regulation","Public and national interest will be protected through regulations that ensure that information exchange is fact-based and prevent improper use that fans social unrest or creates law and order breaches.",""],[1,"216","2","Right to Information Act Implementation","The PP2041 will implement the provisions of the Right to Information Act that supports the growth of an informed and democratic society.",""]],"36":[[1,"24","3","Communications Sector Modernization Strategy","PP2041 will build on the success of PP2021 and continue to modernize communications in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"24","3","Private Telecommunications Investment Support","The PP2041 strategy will continue to provide policy and institutional support to private investment in expanding telecommunications network and services,",""],[1,"24","3","Private Media Expansion Support","boost the expansion of private print, audio and video media,",""],[1,"24","3","Right to Information Act Implementation","The PP2041 will implement the provisions of the Right to Information Act that supports the growth of an informed and democratic society.",""],[1,"54","7","Right to Information Act Implementation and Institutional Capacity Enhancement","Transparency can be increased through the implementation of the Right to Information Act (RTI) 2009 by enhancing institutional capacity",""]],"37":[[1,"14","2","Ease of Doing Business and Foreign Investment Attraction Reform","On the capital account, emphasis will be put on enhancing the 'ease of doing business' for attracting greater direct foreign investment to finance infrastructure and manufacturing investments.",""],[1,"14","4","Investment Expansion to Support Growth","the sharp rise in investment projected in the PP2041 period will be supported by a significant increase in domestic savings, remittance inflows and direct foreign investments",""],[1,"19","2","Public-Private Competitiveness Partnership","a harmonious public-private endeavour has to be developed in Bangladesh in the following priority tasks: Easing infrastructure constraints; Enhancing the quality of the workforce; Investing in R&D to promote innovation at every stage of production; Improving the business climate and reducing the costs of doing business; Mobilizing the large amounts of financing needed for physical and social infrastructure; Integration with Global Value Chains; and Ensuring environmental sustainability and climate resilience.",""],[1,"50","2","Investment Attraction and Capital Market Strengthening","the government has been trying to make Bangladesh a more attractive investment destination, especially through organizations/agencies like the Bangladesh Investment Development Authority (BIDA), Special Economic Zones (SEZs), and Export Processing Zones (EPZs).",""],[1,"50","2","Stock Exchange and Equity Market Strengthening","These bourses will have to be strengthened so that equity markets in the future play a much larger role in mobilizing investible resources thereby reducing the burden on the banking system alone.",""],[1,"50","4","Market Regulation and Entry Barrier Reduction","the following goals will be pursued: (iv) marketing regulations ensuring operation of the free market principles with appropriate checks and balances removing all barriers to entry",""],[1,"65","6","Investment Rate Increase Strategy","higher growth in the Perspective Plan is also predicated upon a substantial increase in the investment rate in the economy from the benchmark level of 33% of GDP in FY20, to 41% in FY31, reaching 46.9% in FY41, averaging 41% of GDP during the Plan period.",""],[1,"65","6","Innovation-Led Productivity Growth Initiative","In the second decade, however, growth acceleration will be fueled by innovation-led productivity growth supported with adequate levels of investment and higher-skilled labour force.",""],[1,"65","7","Foreign Direct Investment Expansion","foreign direct investment is expected to play an incrementally larger role in private investment over time, contributing at least 3% of GDP.",""],[1,"67","4","Development of New Credit and Equity Market Instruments","the introduction and promotion of newer dimensions in credit and equity markets, such as debt trading and debt securitization, venture capital and private equity funds, will be promoted",""],[1,"67","4","Partial Guarantee Scheme for SMEs","partial guarantee scheme for SME will be initiated such that MSMEs can raise money from the market",""],[1,"70","2","Productivity Enhancement Investment and Innovation Promotion","The strategies for productivity enhancement include investment in Quality Education, Information Communications Technology, Scientific advancement, Research and Development.",""],[1,"70","2","Public-Private Collaboration for Productivity Enhancement","Furthermore, a joint public and private sector collaboration will be encouraged.",""],[1,"70","4","Private Sector-Led Growth Strategy","The Government is fully committed to letting the private sector to be the growth driver.",""],[1,"70","4","Public Infrastructure Investment to Crowd in Private Investment","The massive public investment in infrastructure undertaken during the past ten years will crowd in private investment and give it the boost that was missing for some time.",""],[1,"70","5","Supporting Infrastructure and Structural Reform Package for Private Investment","Key areas of supporting infrastructure and appropriate political and structural reforms that will drive private investment in the future include: (i) adequate energy supply including electricity and gas (or LNG); (ii) infrastructure including roads, railways, bridges, embankments and dykes; (iii) telecommunications; (iv) ports; (v) legal and administrative systems including property rights issues; (vi) socioeconomic environment including law and order situation; and (vii) sound monetary policy and sustainable management of public finances.",""]],"38":[[1,"186","7","Bangabandhu Hi-Tech Park Development","Progress is being made in developing Bangabandhu Hi-Tech Park on 355 acres of land at Kaliakoir.",""],[1,"186","7","Software Technology Park at Janata Tower","Software Technology Park at Janata Tower is located in the heart of the Dhaka city.",""],[1,"186","7","High-Tech Park Development in Rajshahi and Sylhet","Moreover, additional high-tech parks are being developed at Rajshahi and Sylhet, and 12 IT parks are being developed at 12 districts.",""],[1,"187","1","Sheikh Hasina Software Technology Park Operations","Sheikh Hasina Software Technology Park at Jashore has commenced the operation.",""],[1,"199","14","High-Tech and Software Park Development","Initiation of development of high-tech and software parks",""]],"39":[[1,"184","5","Digital Technology for Private Sector Competitiveness","Making the private sector and market more productive and competitive through the use of digital technology.",""],[1,"187","4","ICT Industry Target Achievement Strategy","The momentum of the progress should be maintained so that within the stipulated time frame, ICT industry of Bangladesh attains certain targets as laid down in Annex 9D.",""],[1,"191","2","ICT and Innovation Industry Growth Strategy","Driving the growth of ICT and innovation industry should be the focus.",""],[1,"191","2","Regional ICT Innovation Hub Development","For example, Cox's Bazar and the coastline could grow as ICT innovation-centric marine, aquaculture and wind energy technology innovation hubs.",""],[1,"191","2","High-Tech Export and Knowledge-Intensive Employment Expansion Targets","In order to achieve 2041 vision, Bangladesh should target in improving high tech net export as a percentage of total trade from 0.2 to 20, ICT service export as a percentage of total trade from 1.2 to 8, and knowledge- intensive employment from existing 8 percent to 35 percent by 2041 as spelled out in Annex 9D.",""],[1,"193","6","Software Innovation Promotion","At the core of this strategy is the software innovation.",""],[1,"193","6","Service Digitization Initiative","Both service digitization and process innovation through reengineering will improve efficiency and reduce the transaction cost, resulting in higher economic growth.",""],[1,"193","6","Process Reengineering for Efficiency Improvement","Both service digitization and process innovation through reengineering will improve efficiency and reduce the transaction cost, resulting in higher economic growth.",""]],"40":[[1,"183","3","Ministry of Science and Technology Strengthening","There is a separate ministry of Science and Technology that is dedicated to strengthening scientific progress and development of technology","ministry of Science and Technology"],[1,"183","4","National Science and Technology Policy","In 2011, the Government formulated and adopted the National Science and Technology Policy laying down the guidelines for science and technology activities and research, institutional and manpower development, dissemination and documentation facilities.",""],[1,"183","4","Science and Technology Research Promotion","Both the 6th and 7th Plans have also emphasized science and technological research to hasten technical progress and productivity growth.",""],[1,"183","4","Innovation Policy Evolution","Bangladesh needs to pursue a well-planned evolution in innovation policy positioning Bangladesh among top-performing countries as detailed out in Annex 9B.",""],[1,"183","4","Science and Technology Output Acceleration","To achieve them, Bangladesh should target to accelerate Science and Technology outputs as laid down in Annex 9D.",""],[1,"194","1","Evidence-Driven Policymaking and Data Revolution Initiative","It is therefore paramount to leverage the emerging data revolution to ensure evidence-driven policymaking to leapfrog progress, enable improvement of existing services and creation of new services.",""],[1,"194","4","Labor and Science Innovation Integration Initiative","This strategic component focuses on the fusion of labour advantage with the mental capacity of Science and Engineering graduates to attain growing as well as a sustainable competitive advantage.",""],[1,"194","5","Innovation and R&D Ecosystem Development","The core underpinning in succeeding with the implementation of the envisioned strategy is the development of a functioning, comprehensive innovation and R&D ecosystem.",""],[1,"194","6","National Innovation Agency","The National Innovation Agency will work to build an ecosystem (see Figure 9.2 below) and conducive policy environment with the support of industry, research labs, universities and entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"194","6","Innovation Policy and Regulatory Reform","It will also recommend and pursue necessary policy and regulatory reforms in strengthening both the supply and demand sides for the successful exploitation of detected innovation opportunities.",""],[1,"194","6","High-Technology Innovation Promotion","The innovation agency will drive Bangladesh from factor-driven stage to innovation-driven stage, changing the focus from export-oriented light industries like RMG and replication- based import substitution to promoting high-technology innovation for making transition and consolidation to a knowledge economy.",""],[1,"196","3","Innovation Support Policy and Enabling Framework","Actors at the bottom (Items 9 to 12) provide supporting policy, strategy, enabling and facilitation roles to create a conducive environment for innovation.",""],[1,"196","3","Government Innovation Procurement and Knowledge Infrastructure","Government policy, funding and procurement institutions (Item 12) provide strategic direction, develop the knowledge and networking infrastructure for innovation development and create initial demand for innovative products.",""],[1,"196","3","Intellectual Property Management and Protection","IP management and protection (Item 9), risk capital (Item 10) and rewards and incentives (Item 11) are equally important to enable innovation realization.",""],[1,"196","3","Risk Capital Support for Innovation","IP management and protection (Item 9), risk capital (Item 10) and rewards and incentives (Item 11) are equally important to enable innovation realization.",""],[1,"196","3","Innovation Rewards and Incentives Scheme","IP management and protection (Item 9), risk capital (Item 10) and rewards and incentives (Item 11) are equally important to enable innovation realization.",""],[1,"199","15","Research Establishment Realignment and R&D Centre Development","Realigning research establishments increasing linkages with economic growth.",""],[1,"199","15","Private R&D Promotion Initiative","Setting up new R&D centres and promoting private R&D",""],[1,"199","15","R&D and Innovation Market Development Initiative","Creating the market of R&D and innovation focusing in applied research, technology fusion, and system level innovation",""],[1,"200","3","Science and Technology Strategy","Five years economic plan includes science and technology strategy Focus on acquiring scientific and technology knowledge 0.6% of GDP for R&D finance",""],[1,"200","4","Science and Technology Integration for Process Innovation","Focus on integration of science and technology in process innovation",""],[1,"200","4","Technology Transfer and Adaptation Support","Technology transfer and adaptation",""],[1,"200","4","R&D Financing Expansion","R&D financing increases to 1 percent of GDP",""],[1,"200","4","Private Sector R&D Participation Expansion","50% of R&D expenditure is undertaken by the private sector.",""],[1,"200","16","Technology Adaptation for Commercial Innovation","Adaptation and improvement of technologies acquired through public procurement for commercial innovation.",""]],"41":[[1,"190","14","Digital Innovation and Business Model Renewal","Bangladesh should get into forward-leaning in taking the roles of attackers, seeking to harness new technologies, and rethinking business models of public and private sectors to catch and ride over digital disruptive waves.",""],[1,"191","1","Innovation-Driven Industrial Transformation for the Fourth Industrial Revolution","The emergence of the fourth industrial revolution should be transformed in favour of Bangladesh",""],[1,"192","1","Fourth Industrial Revolution Policy Co-Design and Pilot Initiative","It's time for the government, leading companies, civil society, youths, entrepreneurs, politicians, start-ups and experts from all across the society to co-design and pilot innovative new approaches to policy and governance to counter negative implications and leverage Fourth Industrial Revolution.",""],[1,"192","1","Drone Applications for Agriculture and Public Health","Agriculture and public health are just two of the areas where drones could make a lasting impression.",""],[1,"192","1","Precision Farming Support Using Drone Technology","Drones might be a big help in bringing precision farming in Bangladesh in doubling farmers' income.",""],[1,"192","1","National Strategy for Fourth Industrial Revolution Applications","It's time for Bangladesh to have well thought out strategy document focusing on significant areas where the fourth industrial revolution can advance the human condition, such as healthcare and the environment.",""],[1,"192","1","Advanced Manufacturing Technology Integration","Although the focus has been on infrastructure, advanced technologies, such as the internet of things, artificial intelligence, block-chain, robotics and additive manufacturing could be fused with existing strengths driving the manufacturing competitiveness.",""],[1,"192","1","Augmented and Virtual Reality Worker Training","Bangladesh should take the advantage of augmented and virtual reality so that workers could be trained in a far faster way than before, and even low skilled workers could be empowered to perform complex tasks in a very precise manner.",""],[1,"192","1","Big Data and Automation Job Creation Initiative","The focus should be on integrating big data, data analytics, AI, and automation in creating more jobs than likely to be lost on the factory floor.",""]],"42":[[1,"129","2","FDI and Joint Venture Promotion for Value Chain Integration","Bangladesh will have to make up for opportunities lost in integrating into global and regional value chains by courting FDI and joint ventures to develop and trade in a wide range of intermediate goods and services.",""],[1,"130","5","Export Diversification Strategy","This must be reversed.",""],[1,"132","10","RMG Export Tax Incentive","The government has taken a very liberal attitude towards taxation of earnings from RMG by having a very low effective tax rate on income from RMG exports.",""],[1,"133","3","Transition to Technology-Intensive Exports","Bangladesh will have to move towards technology-intensive exports and requisite investment in developing appropriate skills and logistics to ensure the future competitive advantage of Bangladeshi firms will have to begin now.",""],[1,"134","1","Foreign Direct Investment and Joint Venture Promotion for Export Sectors","A similar approach is needed in other export sectors like Footwear and Leather goods, toys, and electronics, by courting FDI and joint ventures with an eye on the future.",""],[1,"137","5","Duty-Free Import Regime for Export Inputs","the import regime must be made seamless to facilitate duty-free imported inputs into exports.",""],[1,"137","6","Export Incentive Structure Reform","Second, the incentive structure for exports must be set right (i.e. removing anti-export bias) by ensuring that relative incentives for export and import substitute production are about the same;",""],[1,"138","3","Export Fiscal Incentives Scheme","Like most developing countries seeking to expand exports, the Government has taken a positive fiscal stance in promoting exports.",""],[1,"138","4","Services Export Expansion Strategy","With proper policies and investments, Bangladesh should be able to expand its export earnings from shipping, air transport, foreign students in Bangladesh, ICT and tourism.",""],[1,"143","6","Joint Ventures with Established Global Value Chain Actors","Joint ventures with established actors within the GVC will allow the diffusion of technology, which ultimately boost the export potential of the local firm.",""],[1,"144","2","Support Policies for Non-RMG GVC Export Sectors","Various support policies (e.g. low-cost credit, tax waivers, generous transfer pricing rules) can be devised that can bypass current WTO 'rules of the game', as WTO regulations have yet to catch up with the rapid growth of trade in value-added (GVC).",""],[1,"150","7","Export Input Access Support Scheme","support schemes have to be put in place to ensure that all exporters have access to world-priced inputs so that they compete in the international market on a level playing field",""],[1,"151","1","Export Financing Access Expansion","Access to long-term and short-term financing must be made available to both large and small exporters",""],[1,"151","3","Government Support for External Market Access","Government support to open external markets.",""],[1,"162","6","Industry 4.0 Technology Adoption for Export Competitiveness","Bangladesh will need to play catch up and adopt the technological transformations of Industry 4.0 (IoT, 3D printing, AI, etc.) in order to remain a global player in RMG and other potential exports.",""],[1,"163","3","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion and Constraint Reduction","That justifies the critical need for foreign direct investment, and policymakers must mitigate any constraints that undermine the prospects of FDI.",""]],"43":[[1,"191","1","Early-Stage Public Investment for ICT R&D Market Development","The focus should be on making an early-stage public investment for triggering the creation of a strong ICT R&D market",""],[1,"191","1","National R&D Investment Expansion","it's envisioned that Bangladesh's R&D investment keeps increasing reaching 2 percent of GDP by 2041",""],[1,"191","1","SME Integration into the National Innovation System","Small and medium-sized industries (SMEs) should be integrated with the national innovation system",""],[1,"191","1","Innovation Index and Capacity Improvement","Through this innovation-driven capability advancement journey, ranking in capacity to innovate should jump from 97 among 137 countries to 30 by 2041",""],[1,"191","1","Science and Technology Output Expansion","Science and technology outputs in all major categories starting from patent filing to publication should give a big jump by 2041",""],[1,"192","2","Three-Pronged Innovation Economy Strategy","Government needs to adopt a three-pronged strategy: i. Software and process innovation, and service digitization, ii. Fusion of labour advantage with science and high-tech innovation, and iii. Leveraging fourth industrial revolution AI and smart machines for competitiveness and low carbon economy, as shown in the Figure. 9.1.",""],[1,"197","4","R&D Financing Rebalancing","To have balanced growth of the R&D ecosystem comprising of three major building blocks, R&D resource distribution keep evolving.",""],[1,"197","5","Multi-Stakeholder Collaboration for Technology-Driven Economic Growth","the Government, businesses, international financial institutions, civil society, industry, Think Tanks, and academia are required to collaborate in developing new ways of working with each other in pursuit of compatible objectives",""]],"44":[[1,"219","12","National Economic Zones Development Programme","The government is planning to set up hundred economic zones throughout the country to create new employment.",""]],"45":[[1,"105","1","Processed Agricultural Food Production Promotion","Industrialists and private entrepreneurs should be encouraged for production of processed value-added agricultural foods ensuring quality and protecting them by attractive and durable packaging.",""],[1,"105","1","Supportive Trade Policies for Fresh Produce Exports","This trend will have to be maintained with supporting trade policies.",""],[1,"105","1","Agricultural Commodity Processing for Export","Agricultural commodities like maize, potatoes, tomatoes will be properly processed for conversion to value-added food items for export.",""],[1,"105","1","Accredited Laboratory Food Quality Testing","The quality of the products must be ensured through testing in the accredited laboratories to enhance the trust of the international buyers.",""],[1,"107","5","Post-Harvest Management, Processing and Storage Investment","it will be difficult to sustain the growth of production of these high-value and labour-intensive crops unless investment is made in areas like, for example, the post-harvest management, processing and storage to stagger marketing of the crops throughout the year to match the demand that remains stable across the season.",""],[1,"107","5","Agricultural Export Market Access Support","the challenge for striving to UMIC status by 2031 will be to exploit international markets with investment in areas like packaging, Sanitary and Phytosanitary Standards (SPS), and Good Agricultural Practices (GAP).",""],[1,"109","4","Agro-processing Policy, Regulatory, and Institutional Support","more policy, regulatory, and institutional support will be needed befitting the aspirations of UMIC and HIC, that remove any policy, institutional, legal/regulatory bottlenecks",""],[1,"109","4","Agro-technology Knowledge Support for Value Chain Upgrading","including supply of knowledge of new agro-technology to help produce according to market needs maintaining the quality and safety for achieving national and international standards/norms",""],[1,"109","4","Agro-processing Zone Development under the SEZ Act","the government may provide with feasibility and other infrastructure support under its SEZ Act which could help develop agro-processing zones in different regions with initiatives from the government",""],[1,"115","3","Good Agricultural Practices Protocol Development and Promotion","Protocol development for Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) suitable for Bangladesh agro-ecological and socio-economic conditions should be the major priority as required under the new Agricultural Policy.",""],[1,"116","1","Supportive Policy and Regulatory Framework for Agro-processing Investment","There needs to be in place supporting policies and regulatory environment to facilitate higher levels of private sector investments with incentives to use technological innovations.",""],[1,"116","2","Agricultural Value Chain Development","Strengthening the institutional capacity and reducing financial and regulatory constraints to address the complex production and marketing constraints including developing a viable private sector-led value chain will have to be pursued.",""],[1,"116","2","Agro-Commodity Cold Chain Management Model","For Value Chain Development of agro-commodities, cool chain management throughout the supply chain is to be ensured through developing a public-private business model.",""],[1,"116","2","Training and Demonstration for Packaging and Processing Technologies","Long distant packaging materials like plastic crates, corrugated fiberboard packaging, minimally processed products development technologies is to be popularized through training and demonstration.",""],[1,"120","13","Post-Harvest Management System Improvement","Improvement of the post-harvest management system",""],[1,"120","13","Village Agro-Based Manufacturing Industry Installation","installation of Agro-based manufacturing industry in villages",""],[1,"120","14","Rural Cold Storage Facility Development","Advice to develop cold storage facility into the rural areas individually or by co-operative system and linkage with relevant organizations.",""],[1,"120","15","Promotion of Agro-based Manufacturing Industries in Rural Areas","Agro-based manufacturing industries can be encouraged in rural areas, such as o Jam, jelly, juice, cheese, sauce, pickle, chips manufacturing industry.",""],[1,"120","17","Milk Processing and Cold-Chain Transportation Support","Milk processing industry and encouraging cold-chains transportation.",""]],"46":[[1,"17","2","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Adaptation Initiatives","developing resilience to climate change adds another dimension to agriculture requiring several additional initiatives to cope with the growing risk of climatic developments, in order to ensure food security, and nutrition.",""],[1,"17","3","Climate-Smart Sustainable Agriculture Support","Going forward, the key priorities for the future of sustainable agriculture include strengthening local adaptive capacity by providing public goods and services, such as better climate information, innovative research for the development of heat-tolerant, salinity- tolerant crop varieties and climate- smart production technologies, efficient water-saving irrigation practices and early forecasting/ warning systems.",""],[1,"17","3","Integrated Farming and Good Agricultural Practices Promotion","In order to cope with the changing climate, integrated farming system should be followed adopting good agriculture practices like Conservation Agriculture (CA), Integrated Plant Nutrition System (IPNS), and Integrated Pest Management (IPM) options.",""],[1,"17","3","Integrated Water Resources Management and Flood Control","In water resources, the priority is to scale up existing good practices of water conservation and management and apply more widely integrated water management, including flood control and prevention schemes, flood early warning systems, irrigation improvement, and demand-side management.",""],[1,"67","4","Crop Insurance for Commercial Agriculture","crop insurance for commercial agriculture ... will be initiated",""]],"47":[[1,"103","1","Balanced Fertilizer Awareness and Efficient Application Promotion","Awareness-raising for balanced fertilizer application and popularization of more efficient fertilizer application techniques, can help preserve soil quality, raise output, lower costs of production.",""],[1,"103","1","High-Yield Variety Expansion for Food Production","Food production of this country can be increased through expansion of HYVs and balanced use of fertilizer.",""],[1,"103","1","Timely Fertilizer Supply and Availability Priority","Timely supply and availability of fertilizer will receive top priority under PP2041 to increase crop production in Bangladesh over the next decades.",""],[1,"103","2","Balanced Fertilizer Use Promotion","Although the government is trying to promote balanced use of fertilizers for crop production through the implementation of fertilizer policy and New Agricultural Extension Policy there still exists a high extent of imbalance fertilizer use at the farmers level.",""],[1,"103","2","Integrated Plant Nutrition System Promotion","Crops should be fertilized following integrated plant nutrition system (IPNS) taking required nutrients from both organic manure and chemical fertilizers in combination.",""],[1,"103","2","Conservation Agriculture Practices","Conservation agriculture (CA) practices such as retaining and incorporating certain portions of crop residues in soil may be helpful in managing drought-prone soils.",""],[1,"103","2","Legume Crop Inclusion in Cropping Systems","Inclusion of legume crops in the cropping may be beneficial in retaining soil fertility.",""],[1,"103","2","Organic Farming Promotion","Organic farming practices should be encouraged in order to get safe harvest of vegetables and fruits and protecting soil and water resources from pollution.",""],[1,"103","2","Organic and Biofertilizer Guidance Program","Systematic efforts will be made to provide guidance for organic fertilizer and bio fertilizer use for sustainable agricultural production and maintaining soil health and fertility.",""],[1,"114","4","Timely Fertilizer Supply and Balanced Fertilizer Use Support","It will, therefore, be necessary to ensure timely supply of fertilizers to meet the increasing demand.",""]],"48":[[1,"101","2","Sustainable Fisheries Management Programs","Bangladesh government is implementing result-oriented specific programs for sustainable fisheries management through innovation and dissemination of environment- friendly new fisheries technologies.",""],[1,"101","2","Women’s Engagement in Fish Processing Activities","Department of Fisheries encourages women empowerment by engaging interested women in fish processing activities.","Department of Fisheries"],[1,"118","6","Fish Health Management Strategy Adoption and Implementation","Fish health management strategy, Aquaculture policy, Marine fisheries policy need to be adopted and implemented for sustaining food security and nutrition.",""],[1,"118","6","Aquaculture Policy Adoption and Implementation","Fish health management strategy, Aquaculture policy, Marine fisheries policy need to be adopted and implemented for sustaining food security and nutrition.",""],[1,"118","6","Marine Fisheries Policy Adoption and Implementation","Fish health management strategy, Aquaculture policy, Marine fisheries policy need to be adopted and implemented for sustaining food security and nutrition.",""],[1,"118","7","Aquaculture Intensification and Species Diversification","Aquaculture intensification and species diversification need to be promoted.",""],[1,"118","8","Farm Mechanization and Vertical Expansion of Aquaculture","Farm mechanization and vertical expansion of aquaculture should be the major priority for sustaining and diversifying of aquaculture production.",""],[1,"118","9","Blue Economy Fisheries Exploration Initiative","Collaborative efforts need to be taken for exploring blue economy-related activities concerning the fisheries sector.",""],[1,"118","10","Aquaculture-Based Farming Expansion","aquaculture-based farming activities may be expanded to ensure the required nutrition.",""],[1,"118","11","Private Sector Investment Promotion for Fish Value Chain","Private sector investment should be attracted for fish and fisheries product value chain.",""],[1,"118","14","Adaptive Aquaculture Technology and Fisheries Management Support","Introduction of adaptive aquaculture technologies and fisheries management system for the poor fish farmer/fisher of coastal region through training and farm demonstration.",""],[1,"118","16","Inter-Ministerial Collaboration and Coordination Strengthening","Collaboration and coordination among ministries, department and agencies should be strengthened.",""],[1,"120","19","Seaweed-Based Product Development in Agriculture","Using seaweed to prepare cake, Jelly, soup, roll, salad, organic manure in the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"120","20","Fish Catching and Processing System Improvement","Improvement of fish catching and manufacturing system in fresh and marine ecosystem.",""],[1,"121","5","Integrated Coastal Zone Management Plans","the priority is to implement integrated coastal zone management plans, including mangrove conservation and plantation.",""],[1,"121","5","Fish Value Addition and Post-Harvest Loss Reduction","Furthermore, the development of value-added products, reduction of post-harvest loss of fish, sustainable management of open water fisheries and Maximum Economic Yield (MEY) of Marine fisheries will be part of the long- term strategies.",""],[1,"121","6","Modern Hygienic Dry Fish Processing Facilities","BFDC will take initiative to establish modern shutki mohal in different strategic locations of the country to produce hygienic dry fish.",""],[1,"121","6","Coastal Dockyard Expansion for Fishing Vessels","In order to expand the docking facility for fishing boat more dockyard will be established at different strategic locations in the coastal areas.",""]],"49":[[1,"245","4","Marine Fisheries Conservation and Sustainable Exploitation Measures","Additional developments in the marine fisheries sector, particularly with respect to conservation and sustainable exploitation, have been undertaken.",""],[1,"245","4","Conversion of Bottom Trawls to Mid-Water Trawls","A proportion of the bottom trawls have already been converted to mid-water trawls to lessen pressure on the demersal fish stocks, reduce the destruction of sea-bottom habitats, and to exploit the mid-water fish stocks.",""],[1,"245","4","Seasonal Fishing Ban for Hilsa Replenishment","Temporary ban on fishing in a certain period of the year is being imposed for several years now to allow breeding and replenishmentof important fishes, specifically Hilsa.",""],[1,"245","4","Fish Stock Assessment Survey Vessel Procurement","In order to carry out regular fish stock assessments, the Department of Fisheries has procured a survey vessel.","Department of Fisheries"],[1,"245","5","Vessel Tracking and Monitoring System Installation","Vessel Tracking and Monitoring System (VTMS) with satellite communication links are going to be installed soon in fishing vessels in phases, in order to monitor and control their manoeuvre at sea for various management purposes.",""],[1,"246","8","Access to Marine Resources for Small-Scale Artisanal Fishers","Efforts will be made to ensure full access of marine resources to small-scale artisanal fishers.",""],[1,"246","8","Monitoring, Surveillance and Control Regime for Artisanal Fishing Boats","Establishing a Monitoring, Surveillance and Control regime for huge fleets of artisanal fishing boats would be a top priority.",""],[1,"246","8","Inter-Agency Coordination for Fisheries Registration and Licensing","Institutional coordination between the Department of Fisheries and the Marine Mercantile Department will be ensured to facilitate a low-cost and hassle-free registration and licensing process.","Department of Fisheries | Marine Mercantile Department"],[1,"247","1","Support for Small-Scale Artisanal Fishing Cooperatives","to motivate, facilitate and promote small-scale artisanal fishing cooperatives in deep-sea fishing.",""],[1,"247","4","Science-Based Sustainable Marine Fisheries Management Plan","by 2020, achieve science-based management plan for sustainable marine fisheries through assessment of marine fish stock and determining Maximum Sustainable Yield (MSY) by intensive field investigation",""],[1,"247","7","Seasonal Fishing Ban Enforcement","enforce a ban on fishing during the breeding season;",""],[1,"247","7","International Fisheries Management Participation","participate in international fisheries management agreements;",""]],"50":[[1,"57","2","Overseas Employment Skills and Remittance Productivity Programme","transforming the skill mix and productivity of overseas employment to achieve greater employment openings and higher return in terms of average remittances;",""],[1,"57","2","Non-Resident Bangladeshi Skills Transfer and Investment Incentives","developing specific policies and incentives to attract non-resident Bangladeshis to actively engage in skills transfer and investment in Bangladesh;",""],[1,"81","2","Migrant Worker Training and Migration Cost Reduction Programme","PP2041 will seek to address these constraints systematically through initiation of training programmes for potential migrant workers, improving access to information and reducing cost of migration by eliminating the exploitative practices of the migration agencies.","Ministry of Expatriates' Welfare and Overseas Employment"],[1,"81","2","Strengthening of Migration Field Offices","The activities of the field offices in the Western districts of Bangladesh will be strengthened through higher staffing and greater outreach efforts.","Ministry of Expatriates' Welfare and Overseas Employment"],[1,"81","2","Migration Credit Facility for Potential Migrants","The government will also seek to facilitate credit to potential migrant based on expected future earnings through participating commercial banks.",""]],"51":[[1,"242","2","National Environment Management Council","the government would establish a National Environment Management Council (NEMC) chaired by the Prime Minister","Ministry of Finance | Ministry of Planning | Ministry of Environment and Forestry | Ministry of Land | Ministry of Agriculture | Ministry of Water | Ministry of Fisheries and Livestock | Ministry of Law | Ministry of Energy and Power | Ministry of Industry | Ministry of Transport | Department of Environment of the MoEFCC"],[1,"242","3","Strengthening of MoEFCC Institutional Capacity","its capabilities would be sharply strengthened.","MoEFCC"],[1,"242","4","Formal Coordination Mechanism for Environmental Management","To ensure seamless implementation and avoid conflicting signals, a formal coordinating mechanism between national and local government environmental agencies will be established.",""],[1,"242","4","Citizen Participation Mechanisms for Local Environmental Management","The LGIs will be participatory in their approach and adopt proper mechanisms for allowing citizen's participation in all local issues including environmental management.",""],[1,"242","4","Upazila-Level Local Government Engagement in Environmental Oversight","A policy will be adopted to formally engage local government authorities down the Upazila level to involve in the oversight of environmental management linking to development activities.",""],[1,"243","4","Private Financing for Environmental Services","The PP2041 will actively pursue all these options.",""]],"52":[[1,"13","1","Decentralized Government and Administration Strengthening Investment","Major investments will be made to strengthen institutions of decentralized government and administration from the top down to the grassroots.",""],[1,"48","2","Decentralization of Authority and Resources to Local Levels","people in lower levels of the administrative structure (Divisions, Districts, Upazilas and Unions, in addition to City Corporations and Municipalities) are given more authority (power) and resources (money) to adhere to the needs of their jurisdictions",""],[1,"53","1","Decentralization of Administrative, Financial, and Political Power","Bangladesh cannot go forward and be a developed country by 2041 unless administrative, financial (including revenue) and political power is decentralized to the grassroots level, more formally to the lowest hierarchical level of government structure.",""],[1,"56","2","Capacity Building for Government and Administration","First capacity building at all levels is to be given top priority.",""],[1,"56","2","Decentralized Government Institution Strengthening Investment","Third, major investments will have to be made to strengthen institutions of decentralized government and administration from the top down to the grassroots.",""],[1,"56","2","Local Government Legal Framework Development","Fourth, develop a legal framework that will provide a clear guideline for the local government machinery about its function, jurisdiction, taxation, finance, budget account, electoral process, and central-local and local-local relationship.",""],[1,"97","4","Local Government Finance Mobilization","As the decentralization of education services proceed and LGIs are strengthened, emphasis will be placed on mobilizing local finances.",""],[1,"119","5","Upazila Master Plan Preparation and Enforcement","The Local Government Division will take appropriate measures to prepare Upazila Master Plan and enact the plan through the LGIs so that the villages can transform into rural township in a proper, efficient and planned way restoring the ecosystem of the economy.","Local Government Division"],[1,"119","5","LGI Capacity Building for Master Plan Implementation","LGD will also work for capacity building of LGIs so that they can enact and enforce the master plan at root level of the country.","LGD"],[1,"120","6","Agricultural Land Use Regulation","Sound regulations will be introduced to restrict improper use of agricultural land,",""],[1,"120","7","Digital Land Records Digitization","Digitalization of land records will be undertaken,",""],[1,"120","8","Government Land Recovery Program","Program of recovering lost government land, particularly khas land including already filled-in riverbank and canals;",""],[1,"120","10","Fiscal and Administrative Decentralization to Upazila Level","Decentralization of fiscal and administrative powers would strengthen the Upazila in providing required services to the grassroots.",""]],"53":[[1,"97","5","Improve Quality of Public Spending","Emphasis will be placed to improve the quality of spending by focusing on timely completion of all ongoing projects and by setting time-bound priorities that are consistent with the strategies specified above.",""],[1,"97","5","Strategic Selection of New Public Investments","In particular, public spending on new investments will be carefully selected in coordination with private provision to support specific objectives like promoting equity, eliminating gender gap, and promoting science and technology.",""]],"54":[[1,"223","2","Urban Governance Decentralization Reform","Some high-level policy decisions relating to urban governance, especially decentralization, is critical to move forward with the urban agenda.",""],[1,"223","9","Resident-Elected Urban Governance Structure","An urban governance structure that is elected by the residents, is responsive to the needs of the residents and is largely self-financing with a healthy and sustainable combination of urban betterment taxes, predictable national government transfers, cost recovery from services provided and responsible borrowings.",""],[1,"225","3","Legal Framework for City Financial Autonomy","Financial autonomy of cities is ensured through a legally defined financial framework that involves sharing of taxes, national grants and market borrowing.",""],[1,"225","6","National Grant System for Co-financing and Incentive Payments","the national grant system is used for co-financing or as incentive payments.",""],[1,"225","9","Urban Local Government Legal and Fiscal Reform Act","The Government would establish a National Task Force of urban experts to review relevant international experiences and give a recommendation to the Cabinet for review and approval.",""],[1,"225","10","Urban Infrastructure Financing Strategy","PP2041 will follow a similar approach.",""],[1,"226","1","Property Tax Assessment, Collection, and Use Reform","However, in the property tax, the LGIs have a potentially powerful source of revenue that must be better assessed, collected and used.",""],[1,"226","2","Property Tax Revamping","The first stage would focus on a major revamping of property taxes.",""],[1,"226","3","Local Government Property Tax System Development","Technical assistance will be sought from national institutions to help LGIs develop an effective system of property taxes.",""],[1,"226","7","Government Transfer Reform","Government transfers would be reformed to assign greater transparency and predictability of the transfers.",""],[1,"226","8","Fiscal Devolution and Matching Transfers Framework","There would be a much better balance between spending by national ministries and LGIs based on a clearly articulated devolution of responsibilities and matching transfers that is enshrined in the legal framework.",""],[1,"226","9","Equity-Based Intergovernmental Transfer System","In designing the transfer system, the basic principles would include factors relating to population, poverty, endowment and performance.",""],[1,"226","10","Two-Tier City Transfer and Incentive Fund System","A two-tier transfer system combining equity and incentives (performance) would be used to promote competition among cities.",""],[1,"226","11","Special-Purpose Funds for National Development Goals","The national budget would also earmark special-purpose funds to promote national development goals related to health, education, environment, social protection and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"227","1","Urban Local Government Borrowing Reform","Reform of urban LGI borrowings: Borrowing is not a risk-free option and requires careful management with special attention to the debt repayment capacity of the borrowing entity.",""],[1,"227","3","Local Government Borrowing Facility for Income-Generating Urban Services","Over time as urban LGIs gain experience and capacity, the borrowing option will be opened for capable and strong LGIs with debt-servicing capacity.",""],[1,"227","4","Responsible Loan Financing for Local Government Projects","In general, the loan financing should be done responsibly based on well-designed high- return projects and in line with debt-servicing capacity of the concerned LGI.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"227","5","Urban Local Government Borrowing Oversight and Debt Alignment Mechanism","The borrowing strategy of urban LGIs will be made fully consistent with national debt management.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"227","6","Decentralized and Autonomous Urban Government Reform","The PP2041 recognizes the need for decentralized and autonomous urban governments as a key part of the political and administrative layout underlying a HIC.",""],[1,"227","7","Public-Private Role Redefinition for City Services","A sound strategy for reforming city management calls for a three-pronged approach: (i) redefining public-private roles with a view to strengthening this partnership for better services;",""],[1,"227","7","Urban Service Institution Capacity Strengthening","strengthening capabilities of public urban service institutions;",""],[1,"227","7","Accountable City Government Establishment","and (iii) establishing an accountable city government.",""],[1,"227","8","Public-Private Role Redefinition for Service Delivery","PP2041 will follow the same principle for Bangladesh.",""],[1,"230","1","City Governance Reform and Functional Devolution","Fundamentally, key functions will be devolved to city governments and, in turn, city governments would be organised to best manage these functions - a two-step process that will be sequenced and managed jointly between national and city governments in a strategic way.",""],[1,"230","2","Devolution of Financial Autonomy to City Governments","The other critical reform discussed earlier is the devolution of financial autonomy.",""],[1,"230","3","Fiscal and Administrative Decentralization Strategy","The national task force of experts charged with the responsibility of developing the fiscal and administrative decentralization strategy will also prepare a strategy for organizing the city governments based on good practice international experiences for review and approval by the cabinet.",""],[1,"230","3","City Government Organization Strategy","The national task force of experts charged with the responsibility of developing the fiscal and administrative decentralization strategy will also prepare a strategy for organizing the city governments based on good practice international experiences for review and approval by the cabinet.",""],[1,"230","3","Local Government Rules and Regulations Reform","The Local Government Division will enact/modify/prepare rules and regulations regarding all the proposed initiatives.","Local Government Division"],[1,"230","5","Urban Governance Devolution to City Governments","Under the envisaged reforms the Ministry's role will change drastically.",""],[1,"231","1","National Urban Planning and Reform Coordination","The Ministry of Local Government will take the lead in defining and designing the national urban priorities and related urban reforms and ensuring their proper implementation in close consultation and coordination with the city governments.","Ministry of Local Government"],[1,"231","1","Urban Development Monitoring and Issue Resolution Mechanism","It will monitor progress with urbanization, identify emerging issues and challenges and seek to resolve them in consultation with the concerned city governments.","Ministry of Local Government"],[1,"231","2","Incentives Fund for City Service Delivery Innovation","This will involve the administration of two types of funds: the incentives fund and the special programs funds.",""],[1,"231","2","Special Programs Matching Grants for Cities","The special programs funds will involve providing matching grants to cities to adopt and implement programs identified as priorities by the national government.",""],[1,"231","6","Private Financing Strategy for Urban Services","Two other financing strategies will be necessary. The first involves private financing",""],[1,"231","6","Urban Services Cost Recovery Programme","the second involves a strong cost recovery programme for urban services",""],[1,"231","6","Urban Sector ADP Funding Increase","the ADP funding of urban sector is expected to increase from 1.2% of GDP in FY2017 to 2.0% in FY2031 and 2.5% in FY2041",""],[1,"231","6","Formula-Based Block Grants to City Governments","Most of these resources will be transferred to city governments as block grants or through development projects based on legally mandated formulae",""],[1,"231","6","Urban Incentive Fund Transfers","A small percent will be transferred as incentive funds",""],[1,"232","2","Urban Local Government Resource Mobilization Strategy","The resource mobilization strategy for urban LGIs identified above will play a major role in changing this.",""]],"55":[[1,"15","3","Universal Health Insurance Access","Specifically, the programme comprises the following: (e) Universal access to health insurance schemes at affordable prices;",""],[1,"15","3","Employment-Based Insurance Coverage Expansion","Specifically, the programme comprises the following: (f) 100% coverage of employment-based accidental and health insurance schemes for all workers in the organized sector,",""],[1,"15","3","Affordable Medical Care Access","Specifically, the programme comprises the following: (g) Ensuring medical facilities for all at affordable cost.",""],[1,"15","4","Public Health Spending Increase","The government will gradually increase the public health spending to 2.0 percent of GDP by FY2041.",""],[1,"15","4","Public Health Clinic Expansion and Service Delivery Improvement","The major health policy includes expanding public health clinic and improving health care service delivery, strengthening health sector governance, improving health information system, improving quantity and quality of health professionals.",""],[1,"15","4","Health Sector Governance and Information System Strengthening","The major health policy includes expanding public health clinic and improving health care service delivery, strengthening health sector governance, improving health information system, improving quantity and quality of health professionals.",""],[1,"15","4","Universal Health Care by 2030","In line with SDGs, the government is committed to achieve Universal Health Care by 2030.",""],[1,"87","4","Health Sector Institutional Strengthening","The above progress in the health sector has been underpinned by significant improvements on the institutional front including procurement, financial management and human resources (HR).",""],[1,"87","4","Digital Health Information and Communication Technology Use","The success of Bangladesh in the use of information and communication technology for health is also recognized widely and has drawn global attention.",""],[1,"88","2","Public Health Insurance System Development","Additionally, the whole system of health insurance is a big missing item in the Bangladesh PHN strategy that needs urgent attention.",""],[1,"88","2","Public Spending on Health Research and Insurance Subsidies for the Poor and Elderly","While private expenditure will be the main source of PHN expenses as the country moves up the income stream, public spending on research and health insurance subsidies for the poor and the elderly will emerge as major expenditure items to enable PHN service access for the poor in both rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"90","9","Universal Health Insurance Access Scheme","Universal access to health insurance schemes at affordable prices.",""],[1,"92","7","Health Insurance Scheme Development","PP2041 will establish this system with a balanced combination of private supply of health insurance programmes and public financial support for insurance schemes for the poor and vulnerable population.",""]],"56":[[1,"87","4","Health Service Expansion and Quality Improvement","The government's development interventions in the health sector have always been geared to expanding health services, capacity development of the service providers and improving quality of care.",""],[1,"87","4","Nationwide Community Clinics Programme","The establishment of community clinics (CCs) nationwide is a flagship programme of the government and is recognized globally as a model for",""],[1,"88","1","Community Clinic Primary Health Care Service Delivery","providing low-cost primary health care services to the grass-root community population.",""],[1,"88","1","Community Clinic Health Assistance Trust","The government has also passed the 'Community Clinic Health Assistance Trust Bill, 2018' for ensuring the participation of rural people in health care services and for collecting donation for the Trust.",""],[1,"91","20","Public-Private Partnership for Health Service Delivery","The PP2041 will essentially continue this successful strategy of public-private partnership by promoting private supply of health services for most of the population while also enforcing accountability for quality service delivery and to prevent willful negligence, and focusing public supply for the rural",""],[1,"92","2","Rural and Urban Public Health Clinic Expansion and Upgrading","PP2041 will strengthen and upgrade rural health clinics; extend health clinics to areas that are not well served by private supply; and introduce public health clinics for the urban poor.",""],[1,"92","2","Clinic Staffing and Essential Medicines Upgrade","The quality of these clinics will be upgraded through appropriate staffing and supply of essential medicines.",""],[1,"92","2","E-Consultation Linkage for High-Risk Cases","Taking advantage of modern technology, these clinics will be linked up with national research hospitals for e-consultations for high-risk cases.",""]],"57":[[1,"92","3","District-Level Hospital Care Strengthening","Public hospitals at the district level will be strengthened to ensure access to proper medical care for those who cannot afford private hospital care or do not have access to national hospitals owing to capacity constraints.",""],[1,"92","4","National Hospital Strengthening for Teaching, Research, and Complex Care","Emphasis will be placed on strengthening all existing national hospitals for quality teaching and research and for the treatment of complex health cases.",""]],"58":[[1,"92","5","Public Nutrition Support Programme Strengthening","Strong efforts will be made to strengthen pubic nutrition support programmes through adequate staffing and resources with a view to eliminating the incidence of stunting and wasting by FY2041.",""],[1,"92","5","Nutrition Education Campaign Expansion","The nutrition education campaign will be strengthened in partnership with NGOs to reach out children in hard to reach areas, children of poor rural families, and children in the urban slums.",""]],"59":[[1,"92","6","Private Health Care Delivery System Strengthening","The private sector plays a major role in curative health care delivery. This system will be strengthened through flexible licensing, promoting FDI in health care including flexible policies for use of international healthcare professionals, ensuring full compliance with government regulations relating to the quality of care and rights of patients, and ensuring accountability for willful negligence in service delivery.",""],[1,"92","8","Health Care Professional Upgrading Strategy","The PP2041 strategy for upgrading of health care professionals will",""],[1,"93","1","Medical Education and Health Workforce Training Expansion","consist of higher investment in public and private medical education, stronger training including through the public national research and teaching, instituting health information and exchange and online training with international medical universities, and inviting international health experts for imparting national training.",""],[1,"93","2","Health Sector Governance Strengthening","The PP2041 will strengthen and enhance the regulatory functions and supervisory role of the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare (MOHFW) including the agencies under it by increasing capacity of the relevant bodies, and establishing/updating standards and accreditation systems and legal frameworks to ensure quality healthcare services including drug administration in both public and private sectors.","Ministry of Health and Family Welfare (MOHFW)"],[1,"93","3","Health Information System Strengthening","PP2041 will improve the health MIS through scaling up of the routine health information system along with e-Health, timely qualitative reporting from all reporting units of both public and private sectors, capacity building of health managers and appropriate use of information technology.",""],[1,"93","4","Medical Waste Disposal System Development","PP2041 will place emphasis on the development of a well- thought out medical waste disposal system available to ensure public health safety.",""],[1,"93","5","Private Investment and Quality Control Support for Pharmaceutical Industry","PP2041 will build on this experience and strengthen support for private investment and quality control for drug manufacturing and distribution through strengthened testing and certification process.",""],[1,"93","6","Increase Public Health Spending","PP 2041 will seek to increase public healthcare spending from 0.7% of GDP now to at least 1.5% of GDP by FY2031 and 2.0% of GDP by FY2041.",""]],"60":[[1,"170","3","Universal Electricity Access Initiative","Ensure sustained access for all to electricity irrespective of location and availability of other energy sources.",""],[1,"173","4","Balanced Power Sector Investment in Generation, Transmission and Distribution","PP2041 will place strong emphasis to this so that there is no waste in terms of idle generation capacity and district-level power constraint to development is eliminated.",""],[1,"173","4","Strengthening the Rural Electrification Program","Considerable emphasis will be given to further strengthening the Rural Electrification Program.",""],[1,"173","5","Power Utility Operating Efficiency Improvement","PP2041 will seek to address these concerns by improving operating practices in terms of timely availability of primary fuel, efficient maintenance practices and better management.",""]],"61":[[1,"22","2","Renewable Energy Development Strategy","developing renewable energy will be a key focus of PP2041 strategy.",""],[1,"173","2","Renewable Energy Policy and SREDA Strengthening","The PP2041 will put a strong emphasis on the development of renewable energy.",""],[1,"173","2","Renewable Energy Incentive Programmes","Incentive programs will be developed to encourage private investment in renewable energy and to encourage households for the adoption of clean energy technology.",""],[1,"173","2","Alternative Renewable Energy Options Exploration","Also several options will be explored to increase the share of renewable energy such as off-shore wind, tidal energy, waste to energy etc.",""]],"62":[[1,"168","9","Power Sector Corporate Culture Reform","Introduce a new corporate culture in the power sector entities.",""],[1,"168","12","Private Sector Finance Mobilization","Increase private sector participation to mobilise finance.",""],[1,"168","13","Least-Cost Electricity Pricing Policy","Ensure a reasonable and affordable price for electricity by pursuing least-cost options.",""],[1,"169","6","Energy Efficiency and System Loss Reduction","Increase efficiency of energy use as well as reducing the system loss",""],[1,"169","11","Private Sector Energy Supply Investment Promotion","Increase private sector investments in electricity, gas, and other energy supply",""],[1,"170","5","National Energy Security and Regional Power Trade Strategy","Ensure 100% energy security with a balanced combination of efficient domestic supply with competitively-priced power imports and exports from regional neighbours including India, Nepal and Bhutan and primary energy from the rest of the world.",""],[1,"170","8","Power Sector Financial Sustainability Reform","On the financing side, a core objective is to ensure the financial sustainability of the power sector so that the power sector earns a reasonable rate of return on assets as is common in upper-middle-income and high-income countries.",""],[1,"171","14","Private Sector Energy Supply Investment Promotion","Increase private sector investments in electricity, gas, and other energy supply",""],[1,"174","1","Private Power Generation Promotion Strategy","The PP2041 will build on this to further stimulate the role of private power generation.",""],[1,"174","1","Private Electricity Distribution Reform","it will be appropriate to explore options for private distribution of electricity to promote efficiency and competition.",""],[1,"174","1","Bangladesh Energy Regulatory Commission Strengthening","the role of the Bangladesh Energy Regulatory Commission (BERC) will be strengthened through greater autonomy and quality staffing to enable proper regulation and pricing of power and energy services.",""],[1,"174","2","Private Renewable Energy Supply Expansion","Another focus of the PP2041 strategy will be the encouragement of renewable energy supply by private producers, including supply to the grid as well as direct sales to households.",""],[1,"174","2","IDCOL Solar Housing and Irrigation Schemes","The solar housing schemes and solar irrigation supported by IDCOL are important examples of non-grid supply of renewable energy.",""],[1,"174","2","Oil and Gas Market Deregulation and Pricing Reform","PP2041 also intends to broaden the role of the private sector in the development of the oil and gas markets through deregulation and pricing reforms.",""],[1,"174","3","Expansion of Cross-Border Power Imports","Under PP2041, Bangladesh will seek to considerably expand power import options at competitive prices from neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"174","3","Regional Electricity Trading Promotion","PP2041 will actively explore and promote trading options with neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"174","4","Energy Pricing Reform for Power Sector Financial Sustainability","Ensure proper energy pricing policy: Sound energy pricing policy is essential to ensure efficient use of this expensive and critical resource, to finance public investment, provide high-quality service to consumers, to promote private investment, and to ensure environmental protection.",""],[1,"175","1","Fossil Fuel Pricing Reform","PP2041 will ensure that all fossil fuels are properly priced to eliminate the subsidy.",""],[1,"175","1","Carbon Tax Adoption","consideration will also be given to the adoption of a carbon tax to reduce carbon emission from the use of fossil fuel and to promote investment.",""],[1,"175","2","Strengthening of Power and Energy Institutions","PP2041 will continue to secure further gains in all these areas.",""],[1,"175","2","Strengthening of Energy Regulatory Agencies","energy regulatory agencies will also be strengthened.",""],[1,"175","2","Autonomization and Staffing of Bangladesh Energy Regulatory Commission","The BERC will be made fully autonomous and staffed adequately to play its natural role in a competitive and deregulated market to safeguard the public interest and promote healthy competition.",""],[1,"175","3","Strengthening of SREDA for Renewable Energy and Energy Efficiency","Its role and effectiveness in expanding the reach of renewable energy and securing energy efficiency will be further strengthened through capacity building, policy changes and financing.",""],[1,"176","3","Public Energy Utility Financial Performance Reform","The power and energy sector strategy provides for a similar financial performance target for Bangladesh public energy utilities.",""]],"63":[[1,"170","6","Energy Strategy for Environmentally Consistent Supply","Develop an energy strategy that ensures the consistency of energy production and supply with environmental protection.",""],[1,"170","7","National Petroleum Pipeline Network Development","Develop pipeline network throughout the country for transportation of petroleum products in a faster, safer, easier and environment-friendly manner.",""],[1,"171","15","Petroleum Pipeline Installation","Installation of petroleum pipeline",""],[1,"172","1","Natural Gas Exploration Partnership Programme","efforts will continue to discover new fields in partnership with international oil companies.",""],[1,"172","2","LNG Import Strategy Implementation","Implementation of the LNG strategy is underway.",""],[1,"172","2","Onshore LNG Terminal Development","Petrobangla has also a plan to set up an onshore LNG Terminal with a capacity of 7.5 million tons a year having an expansion provision up to 15 million tons a year.",""],[1,"172","2","Master Sales Purchase Agreement Signing","signing of Master Sales Purchase Agreements (MSPA) with shortlisted suppliers/traders is underway.",""],[1,"172","2","LNG Expansion Program Monitoring and Strategy Update","PP2041 will monitor progress with LNG expansion program and update strategy as necessary in the context of the PSMP.",""],[1,"173","3","Primary Fuel Infrastructure Development","Develop the required infrastructure for primary fuel: Both LNG and imported coal are heavily infrastructure-dependent fuel options.",""],[1,"173","3","Domestic Oil Refining Capacity Expansion","Additionally, PP2041 will substantially expand the domestic oil refining capacity",""],[1,"173","3","National Petroleum Pipeline Installation","and will focus on installing petroleum pipeline throughout the country to ensure quick and easy supply of oil to the demand point along with adequate safety measures to protect the environment.",""]],"64":[[1,"172","3","Ultra-Supercritical Coal Power Technology Adoption","At present, ultra-supercritical technology is being used in this regard.",""],[1,"172","3","Dighipara Underground Coal Mine Development Study Project","Besides, a study project is going on to develop another underground coal mine at Dighipara, Dinajpur with a target production of 3 million tons per year.",""],[1,"172","3","Jamalganj and Khalaspir Coal Field Development Plan","Petrobangla has a plan to develop other two coal fields at Jamalganj and Khalaspir by the year 2041.","Petrobangla"],[1,"172","3","Rampal Power Project","Several programs are underway, like the Rampal Power Project using imported coal, and the Matarbari Coal Transhipment Terminal (CTT).",""],[1,"172","3","Matarbari Coal Transhipment Terminal","Several programs are underway, like the Rampal Power Project using imported coal, and the Matarbari Coal Transhipment Terminal (CTT).",""],[1,"172","3","Phased Coal Strategy Development","So, a phased approach will be used.",""],[1,"172","4","Rooppur Nuclear Power Project Fast-Track Implementation","The government has put the Nuclear Power Project at Rooppur under its fast track project list for speedy",""],[1,"173","1","Nuclear Power Project Development","Agreements have been signed with the Russian Federation for installing 2400 MW nuclear power project in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"173","1","Nuclear Safety and Waste Disposal Oversight","The government has already held discussions with the international nuclear oversight organization on matters related to safety and safe disposal of nuclear waste.",""],[1,"173","1","Nuclear Power Standards Review","In developing the nuclear power option, the PP2041 will carefully review experience with nuclear power to ensure internationally acceptable levels of operation and safety standards.",""]],"65":[[1,"88","4","Non-Formal Education Coverage Expansion","Progress with increasing the coverage of NFE continued under the PP2021, but there are important institutional constraints that need to be addressed to improve effectiveness5.",""],[1,"95","3","Non-Formal Education Delivery Strengthening","PP2041 will give the highest priority to implementing the government's policy of education for all including the elimination of adult illiteracy by strengthening the delivery of non-formal education.",""],[1,"95","3","Community-Based Learning Centres Network","establish a community-based network of learning centres in order to create scope for ICT based continuing and lifelong learning",""],[1,"95","3","Second Chance Schooling Expansion","continue with \"second chance\" schooling",""],[1,"95","3","Effective Skills Training Expansion","extend opportunities for effective skill training",""],[1,"95","3","Non-Formal Education Strategy Implementation Strengthening","strengthening of delivering all aspects of the non-formal education strategy",""],[1,"95","3","Non-Formal Education Board Establishment","establish non-formal Education Board",""]],"66":[[1,"94","6","Madrassa Education Mainstreaming and Quality Improvement","The madrassa education will be brought into the fold of mainstream education with proper accreditation and focus on curriculum that allows learning of science, maths, English and ICT skills.",""],[1,"94","6","Madrassa Facilities and Teaching Resources Upgrade","Attention will be given to improve the quality of madrassa education through upgrading of school facilities, teaching professionals, books and supplies and ICT facilities.",""]],"67":[[1,"89","1","Strategic Plan for Higher Education Expansion","To further accelerate the expansion of tertiary education, the government in 2017 adopted the Strategic Plan for Higher Education in Bangladesh: 2017- 2031.",""],[1,"95","1","Post-Secondary Two-Year Education Expansion","Subsequently, effort will be expanded for post-secondary additional 2-year education.",""],[1,"95","4","Private Sector-Led Higher Education Provision","Education beyond 12 years of schooling will primarily be a private sector responsibility.",""],[1,"95","5","Higher Education Quality Enhancement Programme","The standard and quality of colleges for higher education will be enhanced by providing necessary library, laboratory & IT facilities and by offering appropriate training for the teachers.",""],[1,"95","5","ICT Courses in Post-Graduate Colleges","ICT courses would be introduced in all of the post-graduate colleges of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"95","5","Private College and University Accreditation Strengthening","Accreditation process will be strengthened to pay due attention to quality aspects of private colleges and universities in terms of physical facilities and staffing quality.",""],[1,"96","1","Need-Based Public Scholarship Program","need-based public scholarship programs will be provided for students who demonstrate the required competencies and meet the admissions criteria in private colleges and universities.",""],[1,"96","2","Women’s Higher Education Scholarships and Public Colleges Programme","The gender gap in higher education will be eliminated through scholarships for women and emphasis on establishing public colleges for women at each district level.",""],[1,"96","3","University Grants Commission Strengthening and Restructuring","The UGC will be empowered to take a leadership role in strengthening university education and advanced academic research.",""],[1,"182","5","Higher Education Quality Enhancement Project","the Ministry of Education, with the assistance of the World Bank, has undertaken a Higher Education Quality Enhancement Project (HEQEP)","Ministry of Education"],[1,"183","3","District-Level Technical University Expansion","the main focus of the government has been to expand technical universities at the district level",""],[1,"197","1","Specialized Science and Technology Universities","The government will set up more specialized science and technology universities in different regions and invite experts within the country and outside to develop curricula that train students in R&D work for upcoming sub-sectors of ICT industries in particular.",""],[1,"199","14","Higher Education Expansion","Expansion of higher education",""],[1,"200","11","University Establishment and Research Funding through HEQEP","Establishing universities Focusing on quality teaching Providing funding for research through HEQEP project",""],[1,"200","12","Industry-Focused Research Degree Program Expansion","Expansion and formation of industry focused research degree programs.",""],[1,"219","11","District-Level Universities and Medical Colleges Expansion","The government is planning to set up a good number of universities and Medical Colleges at district level to provide healthcare and education at district level.",""]],"68":[[1,"89","3","Technical and Vocational Education and Training System Improvement","The Government expressed its commitment to improving the TVET system through the implementation of the National Education policy-2010 and the National Skills Development Policy-2011.",""],[1,"89","3","National Technical and Vocational Qualifications Framework","National Technical and Vocational Qualifications Framework (NTVQF) has been designed to improve the quality and consistency of nationally recognized qualifications.",""],[1,"89","3","Skills for Employment Investment Program","Another significant initiative is the Skills for Employment Investment Program (SEIP) under the Ministry of Finance (funded by ADB and the government) which has partnered with a number of industry associations such as BASIS, BTMA, BGMEA, AEOSIB and others to impart vocational training with globally recognized skills certifications where appropriate.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"89","3","Integrated TVET Development Action Plan for Madrassa Students","The Technical and Madrassa Education Division (TMED) has developed an integrated TVET development action plan to promote and strengthen TVET activities for the madrassa students.","Technical and Madrassa Education Division (TMED)"],[1,"90","8","Flexible Job-Based Skills Training Provision","Flexible supply of training institutions for all who seek to acquire job-based skills.",""],[1,"96","4","Strengthening Delivery of the National Skills Development Policy","An immediate priority will be to fully implement the vision and mission of the NSDP 2011.",""],[1,"96","5","Women’s Participation in Technical Education and Skills Training","Facilitate women participation in technical education and skills training: Another policy focus will be to encourage more women's participation in vocational training.",""],[1,"96","6","Modernization of Rural TVET Institutes","The PP2041 will pay attention to develop and modernize the existing TVET Institutes with available rural technologies to meet the challenge of the fast-changing economy in the rural setting.",""],[1,"96","6","Establishment of Rural-Based Training Institutes","Attention will be given to establishing rural-based training institutes in high- demand areas to facilitate the participation of women.",""],[1,"96","7","Public-Private Partnership in Vocational Training","The PP2041 will place a strong emphasis on this.",""],[1,"97","1","TVET Programme Streamlining and Demand-Driven Training Support","Existing TVET programmes will be streamlined in line with job demand.",""],[1,"120","1","Rural Youth Training Schemes","Training schemes for rural youths will be strengthened as per their education level, job prospect and family requirement,",""],[1,"132","7","RMG Labor Training","Labor Training: RMG labour requires minimum training that could be easily provided in-house and homed in on the job.",""],[1,"159","2","Youth Skills Development through TVET","Youths will be trained for skill development under TVET with a certainty of employment.",""],[1,"160","1","Secondary and Technical Education Expansion and Quality Improvement","the emphasis now has to be on improving the quality at all levels and types, and further expansion of secondary and technical education.",""],[1,"160","1","Tertiary Education Alignment with Knowledge Economy Needs","the tertiary education system has to gear itself to meet the requirements of a knowledge-based economy where both mechanical and information and communication technology will be on high demand.",""]],"69":[[1,"15","3","Flexible Skills Training Institution Expansion","Specifically, the programme comprises the following: (d) Flexible supply of training institutions for all who seek to acquire job-based skills;",""],[1,"16","1","Education and Job-Based Training Investment Strategy","This will be done with a careful strategy to convert this age group into a well- educated and trained labour force through appropriate investments and incentives in education and job-based training.",""],[1,"16","1","Public-Private Partnership for Education and Skills Training","From both delivery capacity and funding perspectives, public sector alone cannot address these challenges and a strong public-private partnership with coordinated investments and enabling policies will be essential.",""],[1,"16","1","Job-Aligned Skills Training Strategy","The training strategy will ensure that skills are related to jobs and not supply- driven.",""],[1,"20","6","Skills Development Program for Overseas Employment","For this purpose, a well-planned skills development program will be adopted commensurate with National Skills Development Policy keeping in mind skill demands in destination countries.",""],[1,"20","6","Training Assessment Mechanism","Training Assessment Mechanism will be in place for",""],[1,"21","1","Vocational Training Standards and Accreditation Upgrade","Standard of training and accreditation will be raised to international levels by setting a minimum level of vocational training for every trade.",""],[1,"21","1","Training Centre Quality Improvement and Instructor Qualification Assessment","Qualitative development of training programs in Training Centres with appropriate qualifications of the instructors will be ensured, and periodical assessment of their competency and resources requirements.",""],[1,"56","5","Skills for Employment Intensive Program","milestones and targets for PP2041 are built around the government's Skills for Employment Intensive Program (SEIP) program.",""],[1,"57","2","National Skills Development Policy and Strategy","Articulating a skill development policy and strategy in response to structural changes in the economy and global opportunities abroad;",""],[1,"57","2","Expanded Skill Development Investment Programme","following up the policy and strategy with larger investments in skill development;",""],[1,"57","2","Demographic Dividend and Productivity-Aligned Skills Development","synchronizing skill development with the exploitation of the demographic dividend on the one hand and growth and structural change based on productivity growth on the other;",""],[1,"57","2","ICT Skills Development Investment and PPP Mobilization","increasing public investments and mobilizing private resources including PPP for the development of ICT and related skills;",""],[1,"57","2","Female Literacy and Women’s Skills Participation Investment","making additional investments in female literacy, greater participation of women in skill development programs, increased female labour force participation in formal sector employment and creating greater opportunities for women in business.",""],[1,"57","3","Private Sector-Based Skills Development System","Continuation of the above strategy with added emphasis on reducing supply-demand mismatch and unemployment and under-employment at all levels and among all groups; adapting skill composition to changes in technology; ensuring that training and skill development is mostly private sector based as skill development develops and matures as a market- based activity; facilitating selected import of skilled labour to fill gaps; and continuing manpower exports for overseas employment; and making the development of ICT and related skills an integral part of strategies for longer-term skill development.",""],[1,"57","6","Manpower Support Training and Skills Development","2. Manpower support - training and skill development to develop talent supply pipeline",""],[1,"57","7","Budget Allocation for Upgraded IT Education","Budget allocation for upgraded IT education at universities, CoEs and the National Institute for Information and Communication Technology",""],[1,"58","1","Joint Education and Skills Development Program with Foreign Universities","Develop a joint education and skill development program with foreign universities",""],[1,"77","2","Training and Skills Expansion for Poor Workers","their training and skill base will have to be substantially expanded.",""]],"70":[[1,"183","2","ICT-Enabled Inclusive Education Solutions","a2i's interventions have also had a significant impact on the educational sector of Bangladesh through ICT enabled dynamic solutions which aims at ensuring inclusive and accessible quality education for everyone while promoting \"leaving no one behind\".",""],[1,"186","2","Digital Transformation of Textbooks Initiative","Initiatives like \"Digital Transformation of Text Books\"",""],[1,"187","1","IT Professional Development and Training Expansion","For addressing the human resource need of the industry, Government has been making progress in developing trained professionals for reaching the number of IT professionals up to 2 million by 2021.",""],[1,"187","1","University ICT Labs and District IT Training Centres","As part of the program, Government has established specialized 16 labs at universities and 10 IT Training and Incubation Centres at district levels, and launched projects and programs to achieve the target, and 20 specialized labs at universities are in progress.",""],[1,"187","1","Compulsory Secondary-Level ICT Education","The government has also introduced compulsory ICT education at the secondary level.",""],[1,"194","2","Mass Digital Literacy Initiative","Alarming phenomenon such as the proliferation of fake news and control of personal data by mega corporations have to be addressed with citizen-centric regulation and mass digital literacy.",""],[1,"196","4","Sheikh Hasina Institute for Frontier Technologies","The SHIFT is a learning environment to create the skills of the future generation.",""]],"71":[[1,"191","1","University-Centric R&D Integration","Universities are to be integrated with the ecosystem in creating intellectual assets and transferring them into product and process features",""],[1,"196","5","Industry-Focused R&D Labs","3 Industry Focused R&D labs: These labs will basically be in charge of the implementation of innovation opportunities.",""],[1,"196","6","University Innovation Assignment Programme","universities will be given specific responsibilities in undertaking innovation assignments given by councilsthe National Innovation Agency.",""],[1,"196","6","University Research and Industry Linkage Reform","i. realigning academic research establishments increasing linkages with economic growth, ii. setting up new R&D centres and promoting R&D for meeting the industry need, iii. linking higher education to industry through research and innovation supporting the competitiveness of the industry, iv. creating the market of academic R&D and innovation focusing on applied research, technology fusion, and system-level innovation, v. transforming science into technology invention and innovation by facilitating technology transfer and commercialization, and vi. supporting path-breaking scientific research for disruptive innovation.",""],[1,"197","2","University R&D Funding Allocation","one approach will be to earmark an increasing volume of funds to leading universities, mainly through the Ministry of Education (MOE).","Ministry of Education (MOE)"],[1,"197","2","National University-Led R&D Programmes","Leading universities should be expected to lead in national R&D programs and projects, facilitate technology diffusion and pullovers, promote spin-off companies, incubation centres, and open laboratories for R&D sharing, to bridge-in foreign technology and partners.",""],[1,"197","2","University-Industry Technology Partnership Initiative","But this must occur in partnership with the most advanced companies in technologically sophisticated fields, particularly in advanced ICT sub-sectors.",""],[1,"197","3","University-Industry R&D Linkage Action Program","An action program can be launched to promote specifically university-industry links for R&D.",""],[1,"197","3","State Technology Transfer Centres in Leading Universities","The goal of this group should be to set up state technology transfer centres in four to six leading universities at the beginning, with adequate funding and the most competent leadership that can be recruited nationally and internationally.",""],[1,"199","14","Agricultural and Industrial Research Establishment Programme","Setting up agriculture and industrial research establishments",""],[1,"199","15","University-Industry Research and Innovation Linkage Programme","Linking higher education to industry through research and innovation.",""],[1,"200","12","Integration of Academic Research into Products and Processes","Integration of academic research outputs in products and processes.",""]],"72":[[1,"161","4","Inclusive Automation Policy Framework","Designing policies to ensure that automation does not lead to exclusion of certain enterprises.",""],[1,"161","4","Education and Skills Adaptation for New Technologies","Designing policies for education and skill development in a way that the country can adjust smoothly to new technologies.",""],[1,"161","11","Education and Training System Adaptation for Technological Change","The education and training system will have to gear itself to meeting such challenges so that the economy, as well as members of the workforce, can benefit from the positive aspects rather than fall victim to forces of job destruction.",""],[1,"161","12","Digital Economy Transformation","Bangladesh will have to be transformed into a digital economy with industry and services rapidly adopting the technological advances taking place around the globe.",""],[1,"163","4","Education and Training System Alignment for a Knowledge- and Technology-Based Economy","The education and training system will have to gear itself towards meeting the challenges of a knowledge- and technology-based economy.",""]],"73":[[1,"82","2","Balanced Regional Development Initiative","The Sixth and the Seventh Five Year Plans put considerable emphasis on balanced regional development through a range of policy initiatives including public development spending to improve farm production and district infrastructure, improving access to credit, and increasing connectivity between the remote districts with growth centres.",""]],"74":[[1,"128","6","Trade Facilitation and Logistics Improvement Programme","Trade facilitation will reduce cost and increase speed of trade.",""],[1,"128","6","Shipping Capacity Expansion and Lane Development","The cost of shipping will fall, driven by a combination of larger vessels and the expansion of shipping lanes.",""],[1,"128","6","Airport Expansion and Border Control Streamlining","New airports, with increased energy efficiency and further streamlining of border control processes, will speed up trade and",""],[1,"134","4","Port Modernization and Deep Seaport Development","Port modernization, upgradation, and establishment of deep seaports will have to be in Bangladesh's long-term agenda.",""],[1,"134","4","Regional Port Utilization Strategy","Leveraging regional ports should be a viable option for the future.",""],[1,"135","1","Open Sky Policy for Regular Air Cargo Movement","An open sky policy for regular air cargo movement needs to be put in place.",""],[1,"136","1","Customised Trade Capacity-Building and Technical Studies Programme","What is required are customised training programmes to develop some immediate technical capacities and assistance for commissioned research/technical studies for dealing with some of the urgent priorities, as outlined above.",""],[1,"149","3","Complementary Export Promotion Policies and Programs","For effective export promotion, in addition to the export policies, a set of other complementary policies and programs are critically required.",""],[1,"149","3","Macroeconomic Stability Support","Stabilities of the macroeconomic environment, the effectiveness of the export promoting and supporting institutions, and smooth functioning of the financial markets are necessities.",""],[1,"149","3","Technology Diffusion and Physical Infrastructure Support","The government should also take an effective role in technology diffusion and in providing appropriate physical infrastructural facilities.",""],[1,"150","2","Customs Administration Efficiency and Transparency Reform","other aspects of efficiency and transparency will be added to customs administration",""]],"75":[[1,"90","7","Universal Free Education for Twelve Years","Universal free education for up to 12 years.",""],[1,"94","1","Strategic Public-Private Education Partnership","partnership with coordinated investments and enabling policies will be essential.",""],[1,"94","3","Public-Private Partnership for Education Delivery","PP2041 will further strengthen the partnership between public and private sectors in the delivery of primary and secondary education.",""],[1,"94","3","Universal Twelve-Year Basic Education Guarantee","The public sector will have the primary responsibility to ensure that each child goes through a minimum of 12 years of education by FY2031.",""],[1,"94","3","Private Schooling Support Policy and Regulation","Supply of private schooling for those who can afford will be further stimulated through policy and regulatory support.",""],[1,"94","3","Education Access Measures for Hard-to-Reach Children","Appropriate policy measures should be taken to strengthen to reach out children in urban slums, hard to reach areas and out of school children.",""],[1,"94","4","Education Quality Improvement Initiative","Emphasis will be placed on sharply increasing the quality of learning at each stage of the education cycle starting with primary education through strengthening of the quality of education inputs including physical facilities, teaching professionals, curriculum, books and supplies and parent involvement in primary and secondary schooling.",""],[1,"94","4","National Early Childhood Learning Expansion Programme","Early child learning programme shall be mainstreamed all over the country by adopting a programmatic approach to the expansion of early learning.",""],[1,"94","4","STEM and Language Skills Strengthening in Schools","Strong emphasis will be placed on science, maths and language skills.",""],[1,"94","4","Primary-Level ICT Education Expansion","ICT education will be emphasized from the primary level.",""],[1,"94","5","Education Dropout Elimination Initiative","The dropout rates for both primary and secondary education will be eliminated by FY2031 to prevent waste of resources and provide 12 years of education for all.",""],[1,"94","5","Primary and Secondary Education Quality Improvement","Quality improvements in primary and secondary education will help reduce dropouts.",""],[1,"94","5","Education Decentralization and Parent Participation Reform","Decentralization of education delivery and parent involvement in school administration will also help.",""],[1,"94","5","Anti-Child Marriage Law Enforcement and Prevention Measures","the government will ensure monitoring and full implementation of anti-child marriage laws, including preventive measures such as information dissemination through campaigning and community participation and parent counselling.",""],[1,"94","7","Secondary School Intake Expansion","Converting the demographic potential to a true dividend will require two major actions: a sharp expansion in secondary school intake; and imparting training to the workforce, especially the female workforce.",""],[1,"95","1","Free Education Through Grade 12 Initiative","The PP2041 will put particular emphasis on ensuring full free education for all up to grade 12 by FY2031.",""],[1,"95","1","Completion-Focused Basic Education Expansion","In the early years, the focus will be on completion of primary and secondary education (not just enrolment).",""],[1,"95","1","Targeted Education Outreach for Disadvantaged Children","The PP2041 will put particular emphasis to reach out children in hard-to-reach areas, urban slums and rural poor families in this drive for completion of 12 years of compulsory education.",""],[1,"95","1","Education Support Incentives Package","Incentives in terms of stipends, free school meals, and free preventive health checkups for these children from poor families will be emphasized.",""],[1,"97","3","Increased Public Spending on Education and Training","The strategy is to increase public spending on education and training to 4% by FY2031 and to 6% by FY2041.",""],[1,"97","6","Incentives for Private Financing of Education and Training","Public policy will further provide incentives including tax concessions, supportive regulatory policies, and grants to support equity programmes in private education.",""]],"76":[[1,"5","5","Village-Level Modern City Facilities Initiative","we will deliver all facilities of a modern city at the village level transforming our villages at the center point of development.",""],[1,"24","4","Urban Infrastructure and Service Delivery Expansion","An urban service industry that provides quality urban infrastructure and urban services on demand and in good quality",""],[1,"24","4","Urban Governance and Municipal Finance Reform","An urban governance structure that is elected by the residents, is responsive to the needs of the residents, and is largely self-financing with a healthy and sustainable combination of urban betterment taxes, predictable national government transfers, cost recovery from services provided and responsible borrowings",""],[1,"24","5","Urban Governance Reform","Urban Governance Reform: The PP2041 recognizes that in a market economy urbanization will be linked to the growth of economic activities.",""],[1,"25","1","Public-Private Partnership Strengthening for Urban Services","redefining public-private roles with a view to strengthening this partnership for better services",""],[1,"25","1","Urban Service Institution Capacity Strengthening","strengthening capabilities of public urban service institutions",""],[1,"25","1","Accountable City Government Establishment","establishing an accountable city government",""],[1,"25","2","Urban Sector Financing Expansion Plan","PP2041 projects that the investment programme for the urban sector will grow from 2.4% of GDP now to 5% of GDP by FY2031 and 7% of GDP by FY2041.",""],[1,"25","2","Private Financing for Urban Development","Two other financing strategies will be necessary.",""],[1,"25","2","Urban Service Cost Recovery Programme","The first involves private financing and the second involves a strong cost recovery programme for urban services.",""],[1,"77","5","Organized Urban Deconcentration Strategy","The adoption of an organized urban strategy that deconcentrates urban growth into many more urban centres than just Dhaka and surrounding cities is essential for sustained poverty progress as well as rapid growth under PP2041.",""],[1,"81","3","Decentralized Urban Development Reform","The government will support this decentralized urban development through political, legal, institutional and financial reforms.",""],[1,"81","3","Regional Urban Centres Establishment","At the first stage, the target will be to establish at least 8 Regional urban centres: Dhaka, Mymensingh, Chattogram, Sylhet, Rajshahi, Rangpur, Barishal and Khulna.",""],[1,"81","3","Urban Infrastructure Strengthening in Five Cities","So, the main focus will be to strengthen the urban infrastructure of the remaining 5 cities.",""],[1,"81","3","Urban Centres Development Near Dhaka","In addition to that, it is equally important to develop urban centers near megacity Dhaka.",""],[1,"82","2","Urbanization Strategy Implementation","The implementation of the urbanization strategy discussed above will be of special importance to reduce regional disparities.",""]],"77":[[1,"240","2","Fossil Fuel Subsidy Reform","Fossil fuel subsidy reform will support climate change policies and goals.",""],[1,"240","3","Carbon Tax on Fossil Fuel Consumption","Bangladesh will start implementing a carbon tax from FY2020.",""],[1,"240","4","Industrial Air Pollution Tax System","Once data and monitoring equipment are in place, a system of air pollution taxes would be levied to create incentives for industrialists to adopt clean technology.",""],[1,"243","1","Green Public Financial Management Strengthening","Integration of environmental concerns in budgetary management requires progress on green public financial management (PFM) in terms of green accounting, procurement and auditing.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"243","1","Institutional Capacity Strengthening for Green PFM","Institutional capacities in Ministries of Finance, Planning and concerned line ministries will be substantially strengthened.","Ministries of Finance | Planning | concerned line ministries"],[1,"243","2","Climate Change Trust Fund Strengthening","PP2041 intends to build on the success of the CCTF and further strengthen the Fund as an instrument to pilot innovative adaptation and mitigation programmes.",""],[1,"243","2","National Climate Programme Design and Implementation Using CCTF Lessons","Lessons of experience will also be used to help design and implement national-level programmes as appropriate.",""],[1,"243","3","Environmental Financing Strategy for PP2041","PP2041 will focus on various financing options noted below.",""],[1,"244","1","Carbon Tax Introduction","The consumption of fossil fuels like high sulfur coal, furnace oil, petroleum and gas would be discouraged through the introduction of a carbon tax as a means of reducing GHG that contribute to global warming and climate change.",""],[1,"244","2","Fossil Fuel and Pollution Taxation for Environmental Financing","the combination of fossil fuel tax and pollution tax on industries polluting air and water, and households polluting water would generate adequate revenues to finance environmental protection and mass transit programmes such as BRT, LRT and Metro Rail, for the urban areas",""],[1,"244","2","Carbon Tax for Green Technology and Renewable Energy Investment","A carbon tax will also encourage the adoption of green technology and private investment in renewable energy",""],[1,"244","3","Green Climate Fund Resource Mobilization Capacity Building","The main challenge is to gear up capacity to mobilize these resources by following the guidelines of the GCF.",""],[1,"244","4","Accelerate Accreditation of Additional GCF National Entities","Bangladesh would take all possible steps to accelerate the accreditation of more NIEs to enable faster access to GCF funds.","Economic Relations Division (ERD) of the Ministry of Finance"],[1,"244","5","Climate Finance Mobilization from Global Funds","Efforts would also be made to mobilize resources for climate funding from other global programs such as Adaptation Fund, Least Developed Countries Fund (LDCF), Climate Investment Fund (CIF), Forest Investment Program (FIP), Global Environmental Facility (GEF), Reducing Emissions from Deforestation and Forest Degradation (REDD), Nationally Appropriate Mitigation Action (NAMA) etc.",""],[1,"244","5","Dedicated ERD Climate Finance Coordination Wing","The government may set up a dedicated wing in the Economic Relations Division (ERD) to effectively coordinate and access funding from these other international climate funds as well.","Economic Relations Division (ERD)"]],"78":[[1,"25","4","Green Growth Strategy","So, essentially, under PP2041 Bangladesh will adopt a green growth strategy.",""],[1,"25","4","Environmental Cost Integration into Macroeconomic Framework","The specific strategies, policies and institutional reforms include: (a) Integrating Environmental Costs into the Macroeconomic Framework;",""],[1,"25","4","Air and Water Pollution Reduction Measures","The specific strategies, policies and institutional reforms include: (c) Reduce Air and Water Pollution;",""],[1,"25","4","Fuel Subsidy Removal","The specific strategies, policies and institutional reforms include: (d) Removal of fuel subsidies;",""],[1,"25","4","Green Tax on Fossil Fuel Consumption","The specific strategies, policies and institutional reforms include: (e) Adoption of green tax on fossil fuel consumption;",""],[1,"25","4","Emission Taxation for Industrial Units","The specific strategies, policies and institutional reforms include: (f) Taxation of emission from industrial units;",""],[1,"25","4","Surface Water Pollution Prevention","The specific strategies, policies and institutional reforms include: (g) Prevention of surface water pollution;",""],[1,"25","4","Geospatial Data Analysis for Evidence-Based Decision Making","The specific strategies, policies and institutional reforms include: (h) Geo-spatial data analysis for evidence based decision making",""],[1,"25","5","Environmental Financing Mobilization Strategy","PP2041 will focus on various financing options such as: private financing options, public financing policies, tapping the Green Climate Fund (GCF) and mobilizing resources from other global funds.",""]],"79":[[1,"13","5","Export-Oriented Manufacturing Expansion","PP2041 projects robust export growth on the back of export- oriented manufacturing expansion.",""],[1,"13","5","Export Diversification Strategy","new and diversified export products will emerge as export diversification strategy begins to take hold.",""],[1,"14","1","Equal Duty-Free Input Facilities for Non-RMG Exports","the export strategy of the future will take a two-pronged approach: (a) put in place a policy regime that accords the same facilities (duty-free imported inputs) to all non-RMG exports as are provided to RMG",""],[1,"14","1","Tariff and Protection Regime Rationalization for Exports","the tariff and protection regime will be rationalized to eliminate the policy bias against exports",""],[1,"18","3","Technology-Intensive Export Transition","Bangladesh will position itself to increase the technology and capital and skill intensity of production to fully benefit from the rapidly transforming global manufacturing market place.",""],[1,"19","3","Trade Policy and Incentive Regime Reform for Export Diversification","However, it is the trade policy regime that acts as serious constraint to diversification.",""],[1,"19","6","Export Incentive Structure Reform","The removal of anti-export bias, therefore, will largely depend on correcting the incentive structure so",""],[1,"49","5","Export Diversification and Trade Policy Reform","Export diversification will have to be the cornerstone of trade policy in the foreseeable future.",""],[1,"49","5","Market Access Expansion for Non-Garment Exports","For that to happen, not only must Bangladesh continue to seize opportunities to access new markets abroad but also reformulate domestic trade policies such that incentives between exports and domestic sales are sufficiently balanced to give export production of non-garment products sufficient incentives to overcome the",""],[1,"52","4","Preferential Market Access Utilization Continuation","This trend will have to be continued over the next two decades or more but trade and economic policies will need to be re-oriented to meet stiffer challenges of global competition once Bangladesh graduates out of LDC status beyond 2024.",""],[1,"68","5","Export Policy Regime Equalization for Non-RMG Exports","the approach should be to eliminate any policy bias against export production.",""],[1,"68","5","Duty-Free Input Access for Non-RMG Exports","put in place a policy regime that accords the same facilities (duty-free imported inputs) to all non-RMG exports as are provided to RMG",""],[1,"68","5","Tariff and Protection Regime Rationalization","the tariff and protection regime - which is exceedingly tilted in favour of import substitute production - will have to be rationalized to eliminate the policy bias against exports.",""],[1,"79","5","Labour-Intensive Export Promotion Strategy","Bangladesh will need to pursue a strategy of promotion of labour-intensive exports.",""],[1,"79","5","Incentive Support for Labour-Intensive Manufacturing Exports","Other labour-intensive manufacturing exports will need to be promoted by offering an incentive environment similar to that found in RMG.",""],[1,"79","5","Trade Policy Reform to Remove Anti-Export Bias","The most important incentive is to eliminate the anti-export bias of trade policy.",""]],"80":[[1,"5","3","Vision 2041 Perspective Plan","We have prepared 'Vision 2041' for the accomplishment of that dream and a 20 year long perspective plan to attain the goal.",""],[1,"5","6","Perspective Plan 2021-2041","The Perspective Plan 2021-2041 has been prepared to translate the policies and programmmes enshrined in the Vision 2041 into development strategies.",""],[1,"6","1","Vision 2041 Implementation Mobilization","I call upon the people of all walks of life to come forward for implementation of this Vision.",""],[1,"7","6","SDG Implementation Through the Next Two Five-Year Plans","We will be implementing SDGs through the next two five year plans.",""],[1,"11","1","Perspective Plan of Bangladesh 2021-2041","To convert Vision 2041 into a development strategy, with policies and programmes, this document launches 'Making Vision 2041 a Reality: Perspective Plan of Bangladesh 2021-2041' (PP2041).",""],[1,"12","1","PP2041 Road Map and National Planning Framework","Therefore, it is critical that thematic and sectoral strategies under PP2041 are robust and internally consistent.",""],[1,"12","1","Adaptive National System for Collective Planning and Learning","Moreover, for Bangladesh to become a prosperous, developed and poverty free nation by 2041, the Government must play a leading role in creating an adaptive national system for collective, whole of society planning, adaptation, action and learning through collaboration among policymakers, private sector, academia, skills development organizations and development partners.",""],[1,"26","1","PP2041 Implementation Plan and Institutional Strengthening","The next step is to strengthen the institutions, develop an implementation plan and move full steam with the implementation of PP2041.",""],[1,"53","5","Planning Commission Vision and Strategy Focus","In the longer-term beyond 2031, the Planning Commission should consider focusing exclusively on vision, strategies and policies of both perspective and respective five-year plans.",""],[1,"54","4","Synchronization of Five-Year Plans with MTBF and Annual Budgets","Five-year plans will have to be fully synchronized with Government's Medium-Term Budget Framework (MTBF) and the annual budgets so that regular monitoring and course correction could be made as the economy moves towards PP2041 target.",""],[1,"54","6","Periodic Plan Review and Monitoring Mechanism","A periodic review and monitoring the progress of the plan will be an essential part of planning process.",""],[1,"63","1","Long-Term Perspective Plan 2021-2041 Preparation","the Government has decided to prepare a long-term Perspective Plan (PP) covering the period 2021-2041.",""],[1,"65","8","PP2041 Analytical Framework Development","The analytical framework for the PP2041 consists of four linked models: (i) a macroeconomic model; (ii) an employment satellite module; (iii) a poverty module; and (iv) an environment module.",""]],"81":[[1,"13","2","Maintain Sound Macroeconomic Management","This sound macroeconomic management will be maintained under PP2041.",""],[1,"13","3","Fiscal Deficit and Public Debt Sustainability Policy","This prudent fiscal policy stance will be maintained under PP2041.",""],[1,"13","3","Pro-Poor, Gender-Sensitive, and Environment-Friendly Public Expenditure Reform","The other thrust will be to make public expenditure more pro-poor, gender-sensitive, and environment-friendly; to improve the quality and effectiveness of public spending; and to establish accountability and transparency of public expenditure.",""],[1,"13","4","Inflation Reduction and Price Stability Policy","So, the target for the future will be to reduce the rate of inflation to around 4-5 per cent per year and maintain it at that level.",""],[1,"13","4","Coordinated Monetary and Fiscal Policy Framework","This will be done by ensuring well-coordinated monetary and fiscal policies; improvements in productivity; attention to supply augmentation with emphasis on food security; enhanced public sector role in infrastructure and strengthened competition policies in a largely deregulated market economy.",""],[1,"66","1","Public Investment Restructuring for Growth Promotion","public investment will be restructured to become more effective in promoting growth and development",""],[1,"67","1","Fiscal Operations Reform for Pro-Poor, Gender-Sensitive, and Environment-Friendly Public Spending","The thrust will be to make public expenditure more pro- poor, gender-sensitive, and environment-friendly; to improve the quality and effectiveness of public spending; and to establish accountability and transparency of public expenditure.",""],[1,"67","1","Public Investment Expansion for Long-Term Growth","the growth of public expenditure over the two decades of PP2041 will seek, on the one hand, to shore up public investment in infrastructure to augment long-term growth",""],[1,"67","1","Inclusive and Eco-Friendly Growth Strategy","and, on the other hand, make growth inclusive and eco-friendly.",""],[1,"67","2","Monetary Policy Management for Macroeconomic Stability","Monetary management will play a central role in ensuring macroeconomic stability and allocating adequate levels of credit for private sector economic activity/expansion.",""],[1,"67","3","Prudent Public Debt Monitoring and Precautionary Debt Management","it will be sound government policy to keep a close watch on the evolution of debt in order to take precautionary steps if any mismatch appears between debt burden and debt servicing capabilities of the economy.",""]],"82":[[1,"14","2","Cautious External Borrowing Strategy","As in the past, external borrowing strategy will be cautious.",""],[1,"14","3","Flexible Market-Based Exchange Rate Policy","The government has been following a flexible market-based exchange rate policy that has helped exports and achieve stability in the exchange rate, while at the same time enabling build up foreign exchange reserves to a comfortable level of US$33 billion by end June 2019.",""],[1,"14","3","Phased Foreign Exchange Liberalization","Such a phased liberalization of the foreign exchange system would help boost investor confidence in the economy and promote inflow of FDI.",""],[1,"69","2","Managed Float Exchange Rate Policy","Bangladesh Bank has been following a flexible market- based exchange rate policy since the adoption of the floating exchange rate regime in 2003.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"69","3","Exchange Rate Flexibility and Market Stability Policy","The policy of exchange rate flexibility with limited interventions to ensure market stability will be continued over the next decades.",""]],"83":[[1,"16","3","Sustainable Fisheries Management Programs","Considering the contribution of fisheries sector in national economy Bangladesh government is implementing result-oriented specific programs for sustainable fisheries management through innovation and dissemination of environment-friendly new fisheries technologies.",""],[1,"79","4","Rural Infrastructure and Farm Technology Investment","Investments in rural infrastructure and farm technology must continue.",""],[1,"79","4","Farm Production Diversification Support Policy","Policies to strengthen farm production diversity through research, extension services, access to institutional credit and export support are essential.",""],[1,"79","4","Expansion of Fisheries, Livestock, Dairy, and Horticulture Sectors","In particular, the role of fisheries, livestock, dairy, and fruits, vegetables and flowers can be further expanded.",""]],"84":[[1,"17","3","Agricultural Commercialization Drive","Next two decades, commercializing of agricultural production would be the highest priority.",""],[1,"19","4","Agricultural Export Quality and Packaging Support","To encourage the export of agricultural and agro-processed products to the international market, proper packaging, phytosanitary standards and quality must be ensured for high-value products like vegetables, fruits, potatoes, aromatic rice, shrimp etc.",""],[1,"19","4","Support for Higher Value-Added Food Processing","Moreover, efforts need to be taken for better processing of higher value-added food products by ensuring export quality.",""],[1,"19","4","Exporter and Industrialist Support Measures","In this regard, proper support will be provided to the industrialists and exporters.",""],[1,"19","4","Export Monitoring and Evaluation System","Effective monitoring and evaluation will be strengthened from production to processing and delivery for enhancing export and building confidence of international buyers regarding products safety and nutritious value.",""],[1,"19","4","Hortex Foundation Strengthening","In addition, Hortex Foundation will be strengthened to promote diversified agricultural export.",""],[1,"19","5","Services Export Expansion Initiative","efforts will also be made to increase services exports including shipping, air transport, ICT and tourism",""]],"85":[[1,"20","5","Structural Transformation for Full Employment","Accordingly, the emphasis during the early period would have to be on structural transformation in the economy - especially, high growth of manufacturing and transfer of surplus labour to that sector, and reducing underemployment and employment in the informal economy through such a process.",""],[1,"20","5","Worker Conditions and Social Protection Improvement","Simultaneously, progress has to be made towards improving conditions at work, providing social protection to workers and improving the situation regarding their rights at work.",""],[1,"21","2","Women’s Labour Force Participation Expansion Measures","To bring more women into the labour force a combination of measures will be adopted ranging from promoting the growth of sectors that are more amenable to their employment (e.g., labour-intensive industries like garments, shoes, electronics, etc.) to removing barriers to their employment and establishing infrastructure to facilitate their employment, affirmative action and direct intervention, providing maternity leave and child care.",""],[1,"55","2","Female Participation and Representation in Public Institutions","encouraging female participation and representation in legislative bodies, judiciary and administration and all policy-making bodies",""],[1,"66","2","Employment Generation Initiative","The continued thrust on employment generation, promotion of human resource development, and a wider network of safety nets for the poor, elderly and disabled population will address this objective.",""]],"86":[[1,"21","3","Long-Term Employment Strategy for Industry 4.0 Transition","the issue of technological progress and the prospect of automation under Industry 4.0 will also have to be taken into account in formulating a longer-term employment strategy.",""],[1,"21","3","Proactive Labour Market Policy for Automation Impacts","it would be advisable to adopt a pro-active policy so that the economy can benefit from the positive aspects of new and better jobs.",""],[1,"21","3","Education and Training System Alignment for Automation","The education and training system will have to gear itself to meeting such challenges so that the economy, as well as members of the workforce, can benefit from the positive aspects rather than fall victim to forces of job destruction.",""],[1,"22","5","Fourth Industrial Revolution Policy and Governance Innovation Pilots","the government, leading companies, civil society, youths, entrepreneurs, politicians, start-ups and experts from all across the society will have to co-design and pilot innovative new approaches to policy and governance to counter negative implications and leverage Fourth Industrial Revolution.",""],[1,"22","5","Fourth Industrial Revolution Target-Setting Framework","By 2041, Bangladesh will set targets such that the benefits from the fourth industrial revolution are 50 percent more than the likely loss.",""],[1,"22","5","Big Data, Analytics, AI, and Automation Integration in Job Creation","The focus should be on integrating big data, data analytics, AI, and automation in creating more jobs than likely to be lost on the factory floor.",""],[1,"22","5","Education System Redesign for Technological Change","In reality, the entire education ecosystem may have to be redesigned to address the dynamically changing issue.",""],[1,"23","9","Citizen-Centric Technology Regulation","Alarming phenomenon such as the proliferation of fake news and control of personal data by mega corporations have to be addressed with citizen-centric regulation and mass digital literacy.",""],[1,"23","9","Mass Digital Literacy Initiative","Alarming phenomenon such as the proliferation of fake news and control of personal data by mega corporations have to be addressed with citizen-centric regulation and mass digital literacy.",""]],"87":[[1,"50","4","Land Governance and Administration Reform","the following goals will be pursued: (i) effective land governance and administration",""],[1,"50","4","Labor Law Implementation Strengthening","the following goals will be pursued: (ii) effective implementation of the 2010 Labor Law with 2013 amendments",""],[1,"50","4","Property Rights Protection Reform","the following goals will be pursued: (iii) securing property rights including intellectual property",""],[1,"51","3","Judicial Reform for Investor Confidence","A properly functioning judiciary will give investors (both from home and abroad) the confidence which they need in order to undertake and expand their investments in Bangladesh",""],[1,"51","3","Law Enforcement Agency Facilitation Reform","it is essential that they play a facilitative role towards the people, especially the business community",""]],"88":[[1,"52","2","Civil Society Organization Institutionalization and Professionalization","For social institutions, the target for 2041 is that \"all CSOs will be mature high-quality broad-based operations with some as international best practices and all will be institutionalized under normal regulatory and business practices\"",""]],"89":[[1,"48","2","Democratization and Citizen Participation Reform","all adult citizens are freely allowed to express their choice regularly regarding how the country will be run and who will run it on their behalf",""],[1,"55","6","Election Commission Independence Strengthening","strengthening and empowering EC to act independently as in India",""],[1,"55","6","Judicial Independence and Separation of Powers Reform","ensuring independence of judiciary and separation of power of Executive, Legislature and Judiciary",""],[1,"55","6","Election Legal and Regulatory Framework Review","reviewing and strengthening the legal and regulatory framework for election",""],[1,"55","6","Constitutional Safeguards Against Extra-Constitutional Power Seizure","providing constitutional and legal guarantee for avoiding/eliminating possibility of non-democratic extra-constitutional usurpation of power by any force/group including the armed forces",""]],"90":[[1,"80","1","Improved Access to Institutional Credit for Small Manufacturing Enterprises","addressing the financing constraint through improved access to institutional credit will be critical",""],[1,"80","1","Vertical Integration of the Production Chain","Vertical integration of the production chain between large and small firms including multi-national large firms will be an integral part of the industrialization strategy under PP2041",""],[1,"80","3","Policy Support for Trade, Transport, and Personal Services Modernization","policy framework must support the growth and modernization of trade, transport and personal services.",""],[1,"80","3","Small Enterprise One-Stop Support Authority","Bangladesh can do the same to promote small enterprises that provide the bulk of the employment in the country.",""],[1,"81","1","Small Business Development Authority","Another major policy initiative would be to seek to dynamize the small urban and rural enterprises in manufacturing and services by establishing a Small Business Development Authority (SBDA) as a one stop shop for promoting small business enterprises.","Ministry of Finance | Ministry of Commerce | Ministry of Industry | the Bangladesh Bank"]],"91":[[1,"58","10","Support for Centres of Excellence","The government will also look to support the Centres of Excellence (CoEs).",""],[1,"58","10","Centre of Innovation and Development","Going one step further, to drive innovation, the Government will consider establishing a Centre of Innovation and Development (CID).",""],[1,"58","11","Centers of Excellence Development and Operation","The purpose of the CoEs will be: (i) provision of advanced technology facility for demonstration of productivity benefits to the sector; (ii) development and higher-end training of skilled manpower; (iii) providing a platform for research and development for new technology development and technology transfer; (iv) undertaking low-cost automation and other industrial consultancy projects for upgrading of existing industry; (v) supporting incubation of new business as there are good prospects for nurturing entrepreneurship; (vi) providing common service centre for testing, calibration and others as needed; (vii) supporting repair and maintenance of equipment and (viii) demonstrating and creating models of IT implementation in the sector.",""],[1,"65","6","Education, ICT, Research and Development, and Science and Technology Initiatives","The new initiatives proposed in the areas of education, ICT, R&D and science and technology will be key to this outcome.",""],[1,"65","7","ICT Strategy Implementation","implementation of the ICT strategy (Digital Bangladesh Initiative) take hold.",""]],"92":[[1,"104","2","High-Yielding Variety Seed System Expansion","Various related investments are needed to enhance the provision of quality seeds in adequate quantities.",""],[1,"104","2","NARS Seed Research Strengthening","Strengthening of the research programmes of NARS Institute, the capacity of SCA and seed multiplication programme of BADC are inevitable in order to ensure quality seeds for the farmers.",""],[1,"104","2","Seed Sector Linkage Coordination","The bridging of linkage gap among NARS-BADC-DAE-Farmers is an utmost task to overcome the quality seed issue in need.",""],[1,"104","2","Community-Based Farmers' Seed Production Support","To ensure food security and sustainable rice farming, seed industry should be expanded in community-based farmers' seed production group by providing technical knowledge and input support from relevant Government institutions.",""],[1,"114","3","Private Sector Hybrid and HYV Seed R&D Support","under the current seed policy emphasis has also been given to have private sector involvement in research and development of hybrid and HYV seed.",""],[1,"114","3","Quality Seed Production and Certification Strengthening","relevant institutions will have to be further strengthened in order to ensure production of quality seeds/quality planting material at all stages of its production- breeder, foundation and certified seed and encouraged farmer to produce quality seed and farmer to farmer seed exchange.",""],[1,"114","3","Biotechnology-Based Seed Production Expansion","Seed production activities through biotechnology will have to be expanded.",""],[1,"114","3","Hybrid Seed Production Infrastructure Support","Emphasis will have to be given on creating facilities and infrastructure support for hybrid seed production, marketing and development.",""],[1,"114","3","Farmer Training and Seed Extension Services","Farmers training and technical assistance and necessary extension services have to continue to extend improved methods of seed production, testing and storage.",""]],"93":[[1,"110","2","Agricultural Market Rules and Regulations Reform","Rules and regulations will be enacted to ensure that farmers are getting real benefits for their sweat-toiling agricultural products.",""],[1,"110","3","Farm-Gate Agricultural Price Support","Price of agricultural products at the farm level will be maintained in such a way that the farmers get fair prices.",""],[1,"110","5","Expansion of M4P/M4C Market Linkage Support","Support expansion of M4P/M4C (Market for Char) approach to national private business networks in chars and other hard to reach areas.",""],[1,"110","6","Local Enterprise Innovation and Value Chain Integration Support","Support innovation for the growth of local enterprise and integration/inclusion of these local enterprises with regional and national value chains.",""],[1,"110","7","Public Investment Facilitation for Related Infrastructure","Facilitate public investment in related infrastructure through capitalization, anchoring and influencing.",""],[1,"114","5","Market Linkage Support for Small and Marginal Farmers","Policy support will have to be provided to small and marginal farmers in selling their surplus products at remunerative prices by linking them with domestic and international markets.",""],[1,"116","3","Strengthen Agricultural Microfinance Credit Supply","Microfinance institutions have always been at the forefront in providing agriculture credit. This needs to be strengthened and made amenable to the market needs of supply and demand for agriculture credit.",""],[1,"116","5","Agricultural Marketing Extension and Post-Harvest Management Improvement","Marketing extension services have to be improved emphasizing post- harvest management of agricultural produces.",""],[1,"117","9","Farmer-Friendly Agricultural Policy Formulation and Implementation","Farmer friendly agricultural policy formulation & implementation",""],[1,"117","13","Promotion of Commercial Agricultural Practices for Smallholders","Encourage commercial agricultural practices for small holder agriculturists.",""],[1,"117","14","Farmers' Welfare Mechanism","Articulating Farmers' welfare mechanism including improving nutrition and reduce occupational health hazards.",""]],"94":[[1,"114","5","Agricultural Diversification and Horticultural Crop Expansion","Agricultural diversification will allow shifting from cereal-cereal cropping patterns to cereal and non-cereal based high value cropping patterns with value-added product, including the expansion of horticultural, pulse and oilseed crops.",""],[1,"114","5","Development of Jute, Cotton, Sugarcane, and Quality Tea Production","Agricultural diversification will also be achieved by further development of jute, cotton, sugarcane, quality tea production for local consumption and exports as well as that of",""],[1,"115","4","Agricultural Mechanization Promotion and Renewable Energy Support","The Government will, of course, have to play its pro-active role in popularizing the use of selected demand-led agricultural tools and machinery and facilitating the use of renewable energy including solar power in agriculture production.",""],[1,"116","5","Agricultural Extension Services Strengthening Program","The extension services must be able to render required technical advice and management support at the appropriate time and place.",""],[1,"116","5","Research-Extension-Farmer Linkage Strengthening Initiative","The research-extension-farmers linkage should be strengthened further for smooth dissemination and adoption of new technologies.",""],[1,"117","10","Fallow Land Cultivation Expansion","Fallow land turned into cultivation through the expansion of efficient management;",""],[1,"117","11","Farm Production Incentives and Rehabilitation","Enhancing farm production through incentives and rehabilitation.",""],[1,"118","12","Farmer and Entrepreneur Technology Adoption Motivation Campaign","Motivational activities for farmers/entrepreneurs should be taken to adopt advanced farming technologies.",""]],"95":[[1,"125","2","Coordinated Industrial and Trade Policy Framework","In articulating trade and industrial policies during the period of the Perspective Plan these two approaches will be kept in perspective.",""],[1,"126","1","Infant Industry Support Scheme","Furthermore, to develop a globally competitive manufacturing sector the strategy would be to provide support to infant industries with time-bound and performance-based criteria.",""],[1,"142","5","Research and Development Investment for Innovation","Investing in R&D to promote innovation at every stage of production",""],[1,"143","5","Liberalized Investment Policy Regime","A liberalized investment policy regime, which offers scope for international firms to have an unlimited stake in the local firm.",""],[1,"149","3","Governance Transparency and Anti-Corruption Reform","Furthermore, the quality of governance should be improved through promoting transparency and accountability, and by reducing the extent of corruption.",""],[1,"150","4","Inclusive Economic Institutions Strengthening","In order to attain and sustain high economic growth what is needed is building and nurturing inclusive economic institutions that are effective in enforcing property rights, creating a level playing field for small and large entrepreneurs, SMEs and big business, and encouraging investment in innovation, adoption of new technologies and developing skills for the future.",""],[1,"151","4","Policy Direction Adjustment Mechanism","When a policy does not yield results there should be scope for changing directions.",""],[1,"161","4","Adaptive Macroeconomic Policy Design","Designing appropriate macroeconomic policies taking due account of the country's economic and labour market situation.",""]],"96":[[1,"145","2","East and Southeast Asia Economic Integration Strategy","Bangladesh should also try for integrating with East and Southeast Asia on a wider scale.",""]],"97":[[1,"176","2","Deregulation of Power Distribution and Oil Markets","PP2041 will also gradually deregulate power distribution and the oil market to enable private investments in power distribution, oil imports, oil refineries and oil retail distribution.",""],[1,"176","2","Transition Away from High-Cost Rental Power Plants","the role of high-cost rental power plants will be phased away",""]],"98":[[1,"182","1","Adaptive Whole-of-Society Planning System","Government must play a leading role in creating an adaptive national system for collective, whole-of-society planning, adaptation, action and learning through collaboration among policymakers, private sector, academia, skills development organizations and development partners.",""]],"99":[[1,"183","1","iLab Innovation Incubation and Prototype Acceleration","a2i's iLab has been incubating more than 250 projects and accelerating over 60 prototypes from grassroots innovators with a view to scaling them up through public and private sectors.",""],[1,"183","1","Service Innovation Fund Financing Support","Many of these innovations received financing from the Service Innovation Fund (SIF).",""],[1,"187","3","Startup Innovation Support and Incubation Programme","The Government has been supporting innovation by providing innovative startups from different stages from all over Bangladesh with funding, mentorship, network and investment readiness.",""],[1,"187","3","Startup Incubation and Mentoring Services","The iDEA has been promoting startups through offering of incubation space, financing, and mentoring services.",""],[1,"187","3","Private Sector Startup Incubator Partnerships","Alongside the Government, a number of startup incubators from private sector, with rich network of mentors and investors, have been working closely with the local innovative startups, especially tech ventures.",""],[1,"187","3","Hi-Tech Park Integrated Startup Support","With the emergence of hi-tech parks, these programs have been providing integrated solutions for innovative tech startups in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"197","3","Tax Incentives for University-Based Start-Ups","Tax write-offs and incentivized subsidies policies for university- based start-up companies are options to consider.",""]],"100":[[1,"191","1","ICT-Enabled Road Safety Improvement","Bangladesh should target to lower the rate of road accidents by 70 percent by 2041, so that GDP loss caused by road accidents is far less than current almost 2 percent",""],[1,"207","1","Parking and Traffic Law Enforcement with Sanctions","All parking and traffic laws are enforced with appropriate sanctions for non-compliance irrespective of political or administration connections.",""],[1,"209","2","Transport Service Quality and Safety Policy Package","PP2041 will place a strong emphasis on improving the quality of transport infrastructure and related transport services.",""],[1,"209","2","Phased Road User Charge Reform","A proper road user charge will be developed that also accounts for congestion, risk of traffic accidents and environmental pollution and implemented in a phased manner.",""],[1,"209","2","Road Accident Reduction and Enforcement Measures","The government has already taken a number of policy initiatives to reduce road accidents and enforce them with legal sanctions for non-compliance and liability for accidents.",""],[1,"209","2","Transport Safety Standards Review and Monitoring","Safety standards for inland water transport, rails and aeroplanes will be reviewed and strengthened as appropriate and fully monitored with legal provisions for non-compliance.",""],[1,"209","2","Environmental Standards for Transport Networks","Environmental considerations will be given emphasis in developing transport network including roads.",""],[1,"209","2","Transport Fuel Pricing and Carbon Tax Consideration","Fossil fuel will be priced efficiently and consideration will be given to the introduction of a carbon tax.",""],[1,"209","2","Clean Energy Transport Promotion","Clean energy transport options such as electric inter-city trains, electric elevated metro rail, underground rail, electric buses, electric cars etc. will be promoted.",""],[1,"209","2","Port and Rail Service Standards","Service standards will be set for port clearings and rail services in terms of timeliness, online user-friendly ticketing and clearance documentation options, and in-transit services.",""],[1,"209","3","Institutional Reform to Strengthen Public Transport Authorities","The proper implementation of the proposed transport infrastructure strategy will require substantial institutional reforms in the transport sector.",""],[1,"209","3","Public Administration Capacity Strengthening Initiatives","Several initiatives introduced during PP2021 are underway to strengthen public administration including better staff recruitment, training, incentives and performance evaluation.",""],[1,"214","15","Urban Transport Infrastructure Improvement and Integrated Transport System Development","The strategy for urban transport would aim at improving transport and traffic infrastructure so as to meet existing and potential demands, and developing an integrated and balanced system in which all modes (motorized and non-motorized) can perform",""],[1,"215","2","Mass Rapid Transit and Metro Rail Expansion","Provision of mass rapid transit (MRT/Metro Rail), both elevated and underground rail, initially in Dhaka City and adjoining areas and eventually extended to all metropolises.",""],[1,"215","3","Bus Rapid Transit Expansion for Divisional Cities","Provision of Bus Rapid Transit (BRT) that is characterized by dedicated lanes for rapid movement of buses for all divisional cities.",""],[1,"215","4","Pedestrian and Cyclist Special Lanes","Creating special lanes for pedestrians and cyclists.",""],[1,"215","5","Alternative Fuel Vehicle Promotion","Promoting high efficiency and alternative fuel vehicles.",""],[1,"215","6","Intelligent Transportation Systems Deployment","Introduce Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS) initially in Dhaka and then extend to other metropolises.",""],[1,"215","7","Metropolitan Area Transit Linkage Development","Strengthening linkages with cities and towns around Metropolitan Areas through bus rapid transit (BRT) and mass rapid transit (MRT/Metro Rail).",""],[1,"215","8","Private Investment in Commercial Parking Facilities","Commercial parking facilities will be encouraged through private investment.",""],[1,"215","9","Peak-Hour Road Access Management Measures","Time of day use restrictions will be introduced in heavily congested roads.",""],[1,"215","10","Pedestrian Road Development in Major Cities","The emphasis would be given on the introduction of pedestrian roads in Dhaka City and then extend to other Metropolises.",""],[1,"228","1","Urban Transport Development for Housing Deconcentration","Efficient urban transport can be very helpful in deconcentrating city centres and developing suburban areas for residential purposes.",""],[1,"228","4","Urban Mass Transit System Development","Moving forward, the highest priority is to establish a system of mass transit for all large cities starting with Dhaka.",""],[1,"228","4","Urban Traffic Management Improvement","Considerable improvement will be made in urban traffic management relating to traffic signals, strict enforcement of traffic laws, enforcement of parking restrictions, and time of use of congested traffic corridors.",""],[1,"228","4","Private Transport Supply and Safety Reform","There is adequate scope to improve the private supply of private transport options and improve safety standards through tax breaks to bus/taxi service providers and regulatory reforms on seating capacities and quality of private transport.",""],[1,"229","5","Urban Mass Transit System Development","In urban transport, the highest priority is to establish efficient mass transit systems.",""]],"101":[[1,"219","10","My Village - My Town Rural Transformation Program","The government has a program of rural transformation under \"My Village - My Town\" to provide quality civic amenities at rural level to stop migration to the cities.",""],[1,"219","12","Township Development Near Maheshkhali-Matarbari Economic Zones","JICA is going to set up townships near the Maheshkhali- Matarbari economic zones.",""]],"102":[[1,"245","1","Blue Economy Policy and Investment Programme","The PP2041 will seek to unlock the true potential of the Blue Economy in a sustainable manner through appropriate policies and investments.",""],[1,"245","3","Blue Economy Policy-Regulatory and Governance Transition","The transition to Blue Economy would entail fundamental and systemic changes in their policy-regulatory-management-governance framework(s) and identification of various maritime economic functions.",""],[1,"245","4","Blue Economy Development Initiative","The Government started the development of the blue economy under the 7th FYP.",""],[1,"246","2","National Oceanographic Research Institute Establishment","Recently the National Oceanographic Research Institute (NORI) has been founded for coastal and oceanic research.",""],[1,"246","2","Chief Hydrographer's Officer Coordination Position","Also, a Chief Hydrographer's Officer position has been established at the Armed Forces Division of the Prime Minister's Office to coordinate and lead hydrographic surveys and other related research activities in the Bay of Bengal.",""],[1,"246","3","Blue Economy and Maritime Cooperation Partnerships","International partnerships are also being built to strengthen knowledge and strategy for the blue economy.",""],[1,"246","4","Marine Resources Coordination Arrangements","Recently, Energy & Mineral Resources Division of the Ministry of Power, Energy & Mineral Resources has been entrusted with the coordination.","Energy & Mineral Resources Division of the Ministry of Power, Energy & Mineral Resources"],[1,"246","5","Blue Economy Strategy under PP2041","These constraints will be addressed in the PP2041 Strategy for the blue economy.",""],[1,"246","7","Blue Economy Policy Framework Development","Develop a sound policy framework for harnessing the potential of the blue economy.",""],[1,"246","8","Blue Economy Private Investment Incentive and Regulatory Policy","Based on the recommendations of the policy framework, appropriate incentive and regulatory policies for promoting private investment in the blue economy will be adopted.",""],[1,"246","8","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion for the Blue Economy","The role of FDI will be promoted to bring new knowledge, technology and financing.",""],[1,"247","2","Domestic Ocean Survey Capacity Development","On the domestic front, emphasis will be given to developing in-house capability to do ocean surveys with technical support from the navy and the engineering universities.",""],[1,"247","2","International Technical Assistance for Ocean Surveys","On the international front, technical assistance will be sought from concerned countries that have this expertise.",""],[1,"247","3","Regional and International Cooperation for Blue Economy Research and Joint Investment","PP2041 will build on the ongoing initiatives with India, China and the EU to fast-track the research and joint investments relating to the blue economy.",""],[1,"248","1","Coastal Tourism Promotion Programme","Coastal tourism will be promoted through a number of actions including: launch of domestic and international tourism campaign at frequent intervals; establish joint coastal tourism programme with neighbours; develop all-season tourism boat fleet; promote dolphin and sea whale watching tour packages; popularise tourism as incentives/prizes for performance achievers in corporate and government offices; promote ecotourism as part of the tourism; provide investment and tax incentives to tour promoters/operators and facilitators; and develop professional tour guides.",""],[1,"248","2","Blue Economy Offshore Energy Exploration","steps will be taken to tap the potentials of the Blue Economy as a source of energy through off-shore drilling and exploration.",""]],"103":[[1,"247","5","On-board Practical Training Facilities for Marine Academies","Bangladesh has enormous potential for seafaring job opportunities from its 18 private and public marine academies, provided it can arrange on board practical training facilities.",""],[1,"247","5","Specialized Training for Marine and Ocean Professions","Further efforts will focus on navigators, fisheries technologists, biotechnologists and marine resource surveyors in consultation with leading national teaching institutions.",""],[1,"247","6","Seaweed Production and Processing Development Initiatives","A number of initiatives have already been taken by the Ministry of Agriculture for the development of production and processing of seaweeds.","Ministry of Agriculture"],[1,"247","6","Commercial Seaweed Cultivation Promotion","Further initiatives will be taken for promoting seaweed culture on a commercial scale.",""]]}});